00:23:16.002 --> 00:23:16.936
I have anxiety issues.

280
00:23:16.960 --> 00:23:18.686
Darkness triggers my childhood trauma.

281
00:23:18.710 --> 00:23:20.044
Get me out of here!

282
00:23:20.710 --> 00:23:21.752
Hello?

283
00:23:24.169 --> 00:23:25.460
Where did they go?

284
00:23:26.085 --> 00:23:27.085
What is this place?

285
00:23:40.419 --> 00:23:41.669
Mom always insisted

286
00:23:43.502 --> 00:23:45.460
I memorize the Hanuman Chalisa,
but I never did.

287
00:23:47.127 --> 00:23:48.377
Now I'm paying the price.

288
00:23:49.127 --> 00:23:54.085
O dear lord, I earnestly pray,
please keep the evil away.

289
00:24:25.544 --> 00:24:26.544
I can hear...?

290
00:24:27.294 --> 00:24:28.544
Now you show up, my dear,

291
00:24:29.044 --> 00:24:33.502
These longing teeth have waited years.

292
00:24:34.502 --> 00:24:36.835
You mean "these longing eyes", right?

293
00:24:37.002 --> 00:24:39.169
Eyes get blamed for no reason.

294
00:24:39.335 --> 00:24:41.520
It's the teeth that enjoy the real fun.

295
00:24:41.544 --> 00:24:42.794
- Teeth?
- Yes.

296
00:24:43.294 --> 00:24:44.335
Who are you anyway?

297
00:24:46.127 --> 00:24:48.544
A wretched soul, much like you,

298
00:24:49.919 --> 00:24:52.127
Bound in chains for decades through.

299
00:24:52.877 --> 00:24:55.353
Sir, I'm terrified in here
and you're recounting poetry?

300
00:24:55.377 --> 00:24:56.561
You've only been here a minute,

301
00:24:56.585 --> 00:24:58.395
I've spent decades in this cave.

302
00:24:58.419 --> 00:25:00.353
What more can you expect from a prisoner?

303
00:25:01.585 --> 00:25:03.561
But why keep you prisoner?

304
00:25:03.585 --> 00:25:05.270
Why not?
Why can't they hold me prisoner?

305
00:25:05.294 --> 00:25:06.811
Of course they can, you totally qualify.

306
00:25:06.835 --> 00:25:08.020
What's wrong with me?

307
00:25:08.044 --> 00:25:10.270
You've got everything it takes, sir.

308
00:25:10.294 --> 00:25:12.210
You're totally qualified to be a prisoner.

309
00:25:12.585 --> 00:25:13.460
- Right?
- Right.

310
00:25:21.335 --> 00:25:23.169
Relax mate, relax.

311
00:25:23.502 --> 00:25:24.544
It's alright.

312
00:25:24.669 --> 00:25:25.561
I was just joking.

313
00:25:25.585 --> 00:25:26.585
Oh my god!

314
00:25:26.877 --> 00:25:28.044
Sir, you know English?

315
00:25:28.502 --> 00:25:32.919
I've drunk the blood of enough Englishmen
to pick up their tongue!

316
00:25:33.210 --> 00:25:34.502
Ben Stokes!

317
00:25:35.710 --> 00:25:36.835
Who's Ben Stokes?

318
00:25:37.294 --> 00:25:38.228
An Englishman.

319
00:25:39.419 --> 00:25:40.794
An Englishman, you say?

320
00:25:42.377 --> 00:25:43.419
An Englishman!

321
00:25:43.877 --> 00:25:45.478
An Englishman!

322
00:25:45.502 --> 00:25:47.228
Oh, those glory days...

323
00:25:48.627 --> 00:25:51.252
Thamma! Thamma! Thamma! Thamma!

324
00:25:52.210 --> 00:25:53.419
Blood of Englishmen?

325
00:25:53.752 --> 00:25:54.832
You were a freedom fighter?

326
00:25:55.169 --> 00:25:56.544
You were a revolutionary?

327
00:25:57.002 --> 00:25:58.669
Of course, I was a revolutionary.

328
00:25:59.335 --> 00:26:00.335
Wow.

329
00:26:00.627 --> 00:26:01.627
Come here now.

330
00:26:02.585 --> 00:26:04.169
Give me your blood,

331
00:26:05.085 --> 00:26:06.794
and I'll give you a life of indulgence.

332
00:26:07.252 --> 00:26:08.252
Come here...

333
00:26:08.502 --> 00:26:09.669
come closer.

334
00:26:10.085 --> 00:26:11.335
Hurry up.

335
00:26:12.335 --> 00:26:13.377
Come closer.

336
00:26:14.752 --> 00:26:15.919
Come here now.

337
00:26:19.085 --> 00:26:20.377
Agh...

338
00:26:20.585 --> 00:26:21.585
Tadaka!

339
00:26:22.044 --> 00:26:23.044
Let's go.

340
00:26:32.210 --> 00:26:33.210
Tadaka!

341
00:26:38.460 --> 00:26:40.210
Veeran, go get them!

342
00:26:52.835 --> 00:26:53.835
Alok...

343
00:26:54.169 --> 00:26:55.020
come on, let's move.

344
00:26:55.044 --> 00:26:56.085
- No, I can't.
- Get up!

345
00:27:12.919 --> 00:27:15.210
- Easy, easy, easy.
- Alok, close your eyes!

346
00:27:34.960 --> 00:27:36.645
Who are you... the Wonder Girl?

347
00:27:36.669 --> 00:27:37.669
Shh.

348
00:27:39.544 --> 00:27:40.585
Don't panic.

349
00:27:41.085 --> 00:27:42.710
They won't find us in this dense forest.

350
00:27:43.127 --> 00:27:44.627
They will sniff you out.

351
00:27:44.960 --> 00:27:47.585
What are they, sniffer dogs?

352
00:27:48.835 --> 00:27:50.127
Now they won't be able to...

353
00:27:58.460 --> 00:27:59.502
Veeran!

354
00:28:26.169 --> 00:28:27.752
- Alok, you see that truck?
- Yeah.

355
00:28:28.210 --> 00:28:29.294
You need to jump from here.

356
00:28:29.460 --> 00:28:30.160
- Okay?
- Me?

357
00:28:30.161 --> 00:28:31.085
- Yes.
- From here?

358
00:28:31.294 --> 00:28:32.853
I've never even thrown a bloody stone
from this height.

359
00:28:32.877 --> 00:28:33.770
How do you expect me to jump
from this height?

360
00:28:33.794 --> 00:28:35.061
- Alok, we don't have time.
- No.

361
00:28:35.085 --> 00:28:36.252
- You have to go.
- Yes.

362
00:28:36.460 --> 00:28:37.544
- Yes.
- What about you?

363
00:28:37.752 --> 00:28:39.312
We're forbidden from going any further.

364
00:28:39.544 --> 00:28:41.335
You saved my life. Not once but twice.

365
00:28:42.044 --> 00:28:44.036
I can't leave you behind.

366
00:28:44.060 --> 00:28:45.228
They'll throw you in that cave.

367
00:28:47.210 --> 00:28:49.502
Alok, they're almost here.

368
00:28:49.669 --> 00:28:51.044
- Go!
- Yes.

369
00:28:51.169 --> 00:28:52.603
They'll kill you
and throw me in that cave.

370
00:28:52.627 --> 00:28:53.627
Go, Alok!

371
00:28:57.335 --> 00:28:58.335
Hurry.

372
00:29:03.627 --> 00:29:04.627
Go on.

373
00:29:06.627 --> 00:29:07.627
Go.

374
00:29:11.877 --> 00:29:12.877
Hurry.

375
00:29:16.085 --> 00:29:17.085
Look,

376
00:29:17.877 --> 00:29:19.835
I have no intention of dying together.

377
00:29:21.127 --> 00:29:22.567
That leaves us with only one option:

378
00:29:23.627 --> 00:29:25.252
How about
we live together instead, hmm?!

379
00:29:29.085 --> 00:29:30.710
Once you're fully recovered,

380
00:29:31.252 --> 00:29:32.377
I'll take you home.

381
00:29:48.794 --> 00:29:49.835
Girl, you have no fear!

382
00:29:50.502 --> 00:29:52.062
You should totally go for the Olympics.

383
00:29:52.377 --> 00:29:54.577
You could probably bring home
three or four golds, easy.

384
00:30:03.919 --> 00:30:09.895
Though not officially,
still yours I'll forever be.

385
00:30:09.919 --> 00:30:12.585
Yours I'll forever be.

386
00:30:22.669 --> 00:30:28.645
Though not officially,
still yours I'll forever be.

387
00:30:28.669 --> 00:30:32.585
Yours I'll forever be.

388
00:30:36.919 --> 00:30:41.252
Whether or not I am there with you.

389
00:30:46.877 --> 00:30:51.561
Love that no one can understand but you,

390
00:30:51.585 --> 00:30:56.353
Something that's only felt by you.

391
00:30:56.377 --> 00:31:01.186
Something that cannot
be measured or subdued,

392
00:31:01.210 --> 00:31:06.460
Something that even time
can't hold from you.

393
00:31:06.877 --> 00:31:11.127
Love that I have for you,

394
00:31:11.544 --> 00:31:15.960
not just my heart but all of me too.

395
00:31:22.710 --> 00:31:26.710
Sir, Mr. Alok's hit the afterlife!

396
00:31:32.960 --> 00:31:35.419
Now Mr. Alok's entered heaven!

397
00:31:36.835 --> 00:31:40.627
If you've got that kind of pull up there,
why not just call him back?

398
00:31:40.794 --> 00:31:41.582
Huh?

399
00:31:41.583 --> 00:31:42.294
Mom?

400
00:31:42.710 --> 00:31:43.752
Huh?

401
00:31:48.377 --> 00:31:49.377
Alok...

402
00:31:49.835 --> 00:31:50.645
Alok!

403
00:31:50.669 --> 00:31:51.811
ALOK!!!

404
00:31:51.835 --> 00:31:53.544
- My child!
- Mom!

405
00:31:53.669 --> 00:31:54.978
Mom! Mom!

406
00:31:55.002 --> 00:31:56.794
My son's back.

407
00:31:56.960 --> 00:31:59.395
My son is back.

408
00:31:59.419 --> 00:32:00.419
Mom, I'm fine.

409
00:32:00.794 --> 00:32:02.436
My son's back.

410
00:32:02.460 --> 00:32:03.752
Take that off.

411
00:32:04.627 --> 00:32:05.627
Dad!

412
00:32:09.460 --> 00:32:10.460
Oh Dad!

413
00:32:11.627 --> 00:32:14.835
A true influencer, indeed...
an influencer-priest!

414
00:32:16.669 --> 00:32:18.186
Thank God!

415
00:32:18.210 --> 00:32:19.061
Alok!

416
00:32:19.085 --> 00:32:20.186
Alok is alive!

417
00:32:20.210 --> 00:32:22.186
- Sudha... Sudha, listen...
- Yes.

418
00:32:22.210 --> 00:32:25.252
Something tells me he's not our son.

419
00:32:26.377 --> 00:32:29.686
Sudha, he could be an imposter.

420
00:32:29.710 --> 00:32:31.936
Someone who'll milk this situation later.

421
00:32:31.960 --> 00:32:33.440
You mean he'll take advantage of you?

422
00:32:34.169 --> 00:32:36.478
Even the garbage man

423
00:32:36.502 --> 00:32:38.478
won't pick up your trash
without you begging him to.

424
00:32:38.502 --> 00:32:39.710
Who'd take advantage of you?

425
00:32:40.127 --> 00:32:41.210
- You...
- It's fine, Mom.

426
00:32:41.960 --> 00:32:43.294
Let Dad clear his doubts.

427
00:32:43.710 --> 00:32:44.645
- No way.
- Mom...

428
00:32:44.669 --> 00:32:46.210
This won't take long.

429
00:32:51.669 --> 00:32:53.085
So you're Alok.

430
00:32:54.294 --> 00:32:55.377
Alok Goyal?

431
00:32:55.919 --> 00:32:56.919
Yes, Dad.

432
00:32:58.585 --> 00:33:00.544
We used to have a dog.

433
00:33:01.294 --> 00:33:02.710
What was its name?

434
00:33:02.919 --> 00:33:03.919
Moti.

435
00:33:05.752 --> 00:33:08.085
What percentile did you get
in high school?

436
00:33:09.377 --> 00:33:10.377
56!

437
00:33:10.419 --> 00:33:11.252
Huh?

438
00:33:12.127 --> 00:33:14.419
Okay, fine... 55.6%.

439
00:33:14.627 --> 00:33:15.686
- Yes.
- Dad, can we go outside now and...

440
00:33:15.710 --> 00:33:17.627
Hold on... wait.

441
00:33:18.710 --> 00:33:20.085
Back there...

442
00:33:20.627 --> 00:33:24.377
Uh, you've got a mole on your bum...

443
00:33:28.085 --> 00:33:29.085
Here you go.

444
00:33:29.752 --> 00:33:30.752
Pull your pants up.

445
00:33:30.960 --> 00:33:32.720
I wanted to see the mole,
not your dump hole.

446
00:33:33.002 --> 00:33:34.395
Now cut the drama,

447
00:33:34.419 --> 00:33:36.645
or should I share your internet history
screenshots with Mom?

448
00:33:36.669 --> 00:33:38.377
Hey... MY SON!!!

449
00:33:38.835 --> 00:33:40.710
My Alok... my Goyal!

450
00:33:42.544 --> 00:33:43.544
Okay.

451
00:33:46.294 --> 00:33:48.002
Mom, how do you even live with this man?

452
00:33:48.544 --> 00:33:49.877
They say blood recognizes blood.

453
00:33:50.127 --> 00:33:51.169
He can't even do that.

454
00:33:51.294 --> 00:33:52.460
Let it go, son.

455
00:33:52.627 --> 00:33:54.460
This man's blood's negative too.

456
00:34:04.960 --> 00:34:06.169
What's your name, dear?

457
00:34:06.752 --> 00:34:07.752
Tadaka.

458
00:34:08.127 --> 00:34:09.127
Tadaka?

459
00:34:09.877 --> 00:34:11.419
Sounds like a demon's name.

460
00:34:13.085 --> 00:34:15.919
It's Tarika. Her name is Tarika...

461
00:34:16.460 --> 00:34:17.794
She saved my life.

462
00:34:18.960 --> 00:34:21.044
Without her,
it would've been game over for me.

463
00:34:25.377 --> 00:34:28.460
Seems like your "game over"
happened a long time ago.

464
00:34:30.669 --> 00:34:34.002
Mom, Dad, a bear attacked me.

465
00:34:34.294 --> 00:34:35.814
Then she just appeared out of nowhere.

466
00:34:36.669 --> 00:34:38.335
Nursed me back to health.

467
00:34:39.044 --> 00:34:42.002
You didn't just save him,

468
00:34:42.502 --> 00:34:44.127
you saved us too.

469
00:34:44.419 --> 00:34:46.960
No, I only saved him.

470
00:34:48.002 --> 00:34:49.627
Oh, my innocent Tarika...

471
00:34:51.169 --> 00:34:52.169
Why is she here?

472
00:34:55.752 --> 00:34:56.752
Up in the mountains,

473
00:34:57.669 --> 00:35:00.377
her stepmom and step-uncle

474
00:35:00.669 --> 00:35:03.210
tried forcing her to marry some old creep.

475
00:35:03.502 --> 00:35:04.710
I stopped it.

476
00:35:05.252 --> 00:35:07.669
I said, "Nope,
this wedding's not happening."

477
00:35:08.085 --> 00:35:09.936
Sounds like a movie plot.

478
00:35:09.960 --> 00:35:11.728
It's not a movie plot,
it's a saga of cruelty.

479
00:35:11.752 --> 00:35:13.580
- Cruelty?
- Yeah, her stepmom's cruelty.

480
00:35:13.710 --> 00:35:15.419
Good call, son.

481
00:35:16.252 --> 00:35:17.452
I'm glad you brought her here.

482
00:35:17.627 --> 00:35:18.710
She stays here now.

483
00:35:19.419 --> 00:35:21.936
- Here? Why?
- Why you ask?

484
00:35:21.960 --> 00:35:23.520
She saved Alok's life.

485
00:35:23.544 --> 00:35:26.436
- Eight years ago you had an accident.
- Right.

486
00:35:26.460 --> 00:35:30.294
Did we make the doctor
who saved you stay with us?

487
00:35:30.794 --> 00:35:31.794
End of discussion.

488
00:35:32.169 --> 00:35:33.186
She stays.

489
00:35:33.210 --> 00:35:35.061
She saved him. Full and final.

490
00:35:35.085 --> 00:35:36.478
Come on, let me show you the house.

491
00:35:36.502 --> 00:35:37.728
My son's back.

492
00:35:37.752 --> 00:35:40.103
She saved him.

493
00:35:40.127 --> 00:35:41.127
Just like that...?

494
00:35:46.669 --> 00:35:47.936
Hallelujah! Hallelujah!

495
00:35:47.960 --> 00:35:48.978
What is your name?

496
00:35:50.502 --> 00:35:53.103
The hand of God is with youuu.

497
00:35:53.127 --> 00:35:55.002
Hallelujah! Hallelujah!

498
00:35:55.169 --> 00:35:57.210
HALLELUJAH!

499
00:35:59.877 --> 00:36:01.395
Hallelujah! Hallelujah!

500
00:36:02.460 --> 00:36:04.919
Hallelujah! Hallelujah!

501
00:36:05.627 --> 00:36:09.044
Danger looms over India!

502
00:36:09.585 --> 00:36:12.252
The enemy's set a beauty trap.

503
00:36:13.002 --> 00:36:14.710
She says "Hi" to ensnare,

504
00:36:15.419 --> 00:36:17.252
then hooks them with a "Love you, dear".

505
00:36:17.835 --> 00:36:20.877
The young men of our country
are falling victim to Honey Traps!

506
00:36:21.585 --> 00:36:22.835
She'll call to you,

507
00:36:23.044 --> 00:36:24.294
but don't go near,

508
00:36:25.419 --> 00:36:26.603
She'll trap your heart,

509
00:36:26.627 --> 00:36:28.419
so don't get caught here.

510
00:36:29.044 --> 00:36:32.085
Love isn't easy, better know that,

511
00:36:32.544 --> 00:36:36.169
It's a trap, and you'll get caught flat.

512
00:36:43.710 --> 00:36:46.061
Alok, here's your favorite Rajma.

513
00:36:46.085 --> 00:36:46.978
Wow,

514
00:36:47.002 --> 00:36:48.419
I've been dying to have this.

515
00:36:48.710 --> 00:36:49.794
You didn't take anything.

516
00:36:50.044 --> 00:36:51.044
Here, have this, dear.

517
00:36:51.252 --> 00:36:53.270
Tomorrow I'll make 'chole bathoore'.

518
00:36:53.294 --> 00:36:56.061
I'll make any vegetarian dish you want,
you just have to name it.

519
00:36:56.085 --> 00:36:57.127
She's a great cook.

520
00:36:57.377 --> 00:36:58.669
What would you like?

521
00:36:58.794 --> 00:36:59.794
Barasingha!

522
00:36:59.919 --> 00:37:00.919
Barasingha?

523
00:37:02.502 --> 00:37:03.502
Barasingha?

524
00:37:05.085 --> 00:37:06.205
Singhada!

525
00:37:06.794 --> 00:37:08.103
Big Singhada!

526
00:37:08.127 --> 00:37:09.252
It's their specialty.

527
00:37:09.502 --> 00:37:11.669
They are huge.

528
00:37:14.585 --> 00:37:16.752
I wouldn't even mind a rabbit if I...

529
00:37:17.210 --> 00:37:18.877
If she could keep it as a pet!

530
00:37:19.710 --> 00:37:20.919
They raise rabbits.

531
00:37:21.335 --> 00:37:24.020
So, who's in your family besides rabbits?

532
00:37:24.044 --> 00:37:25.210
No one.

533
00:37:25.585 --> 00:37:26.811
What do you mean by "no one"?

534
00:37:26.835 --> 00:37:28.127
No one means no one.

535
00:37:28.585 --> 00:37:30.085
She's a true, pure orphan.

536
00:37:30.794 --> 00:37:33.085
She lost her parents young.

537
00:37:34.210 --> 00:37:35.835
If her parents died,

538
00:37:36.335 --> 00:37:37.561
How did the stepmom come into the picture?

539
00:37:37.585 --> 00:37:38.710
Stepmom, who?

540
00:37:39.502 --> 00:37:42.919
The one forcing her to marry?

541
00:37:43.085 --> 00:37:43.853
Oh, her!

542
00:37:43.877 --> 00:37:46.794
Yes, her.
So, do you have a stepmom or not?

543
00:37:47.002 --> 00:37:48.710
- No.
- No?

544
00:37:48.960 --> 00:37:50.335
- No?
- No.

545
00:37:50.502 --> 00:37:51.502
No,

546
00:37:51.919 --> 00:37:53.679
she means she isn't a mother,
she is a witch.

547
00:37:53.835 --> 00:37:56.596
Then where did this witchy-stepmom
come from if her parents were dead?

548
00:37:56.960 --> 00:37:59.044
Come on now,
this isn't the time to ask such things.

549
00:37:59.169 --> 00:38:00.929
It's the right time.
It's just eight o'clock.

550
00:38:01.127 --> 00:38:02.061
- Well where did she come from?
- Papa!

551
00:38:02.085 --> 00:38:03.669
Rajma, stepma...

552
00:38:03.877 --> 00:38:04.877
Speak up now.

553
00:38:06.627 --> 00:38:08.335
Come on, tell me,
where did she come from?

554
00:38:22.460 --> 00:38:23.710
I'm not hungry.

555
00:38:24.460 --> 00:38:25.353
No problem.

556
00:38:25.377 --> 00:38:26.835
Go rest in your room.

557
00:38:27.335 --> 00:38:28.710
You can have some milk before bed.

558
00:38:37.252 --> 00:38:38.252
Sudha...

559
00:38:39.544 --> 00:38:40.585
Something's fishy.

560
00:38:41.335 --> 00:38:42.686
It's a sap trap.

561
00:38:42.710 --> 00:38:43.561
Huh?

562
00:38:43.585 --> 00:38:44.752
Honey trap.

563
00:38:45.044 --> 00:38:46.044
Honey trap.

564
00:38:46.419 --> 00:38:48.311
She says "Hi" to ensnare,

565
00:38:48.335 --> 00:38:50.044
then hooks them with a "Love you, dear".

566
00:38:50.252 --> 00:38:53.919
Mark my words, she'll steal our land
and property one day.

567
00:38:55.252 --> 00:38:56.020
I knew it.

568
00:38:56.044 --> 00:38:57.044
Right?

569
00:38:57.544 --> 00:38:59.960
This is what happens
if you binge on crime shows.

570
00:39:00.460 --> 00:39:04.627
What's a beautiful girl like her doing
with Alok if it's not a honey trap?

571
00:39:04.960 --> 00:39:05.811
What do you mean?

572
00:39:05.835 --> 00:39:09.811
Alok's a goof, an idiot...
he's nothing special.

573
00:39:09.835 --> 00:39:10.835
Shut up!

574
00:39:10.960 --> 00:39:12.294
My son looks like a superstar.

575
00:39:12.960 --> 00:39:14.080
He's taken after my brother.

576
00:39:14.710 --> 00:39:15.686
Gone senile...

577
00:39:28.419 --> 00:39:29.460
What happened, Tarika?

578
00:39:31.252 --> 00:39:33.085
Is there something wrong with my name?

579
00:39:33.544 --> 00:39:34.835
No... not at all.

580
00:39:35.419 --> 00:39:37.960
Tadaka's just a bit weird for the city,

581
00:39:38.710 --> 00:39:40.252
that's why... Tarika.

582
00:39:41.044 --> 00:39:42.335
Do you know what Tarika means?

583
00:39:44.544 --> 00:39:45.544
A star!

584
00:39:46.794 --> 00:39:47.914
That's exactly what you are.

585
00:39:52.085 --> 00:39:56.169
Your ways, name, food, culture...

586
00:39:56.794 --> 00:39:57.645
everything's different.

587
00:39:57.669 --> 00:39:58.669
You're different.

588
00:39:58.919 --> 00:39:59.960
I understand.

589
00:40:00.544 --> 00:40:01.877
But my parents won't.

590
00:40:02.710 --> 00:40:05.561
That's why I lied to placate them.

591
00:40:05.585 --> 00:40:07.044
We can't lie.

592
00:40:07.252 --> 00:40:08.377
Why not?

593
00:40:09.669 --> 00:40:14.044
A lie that helps someone isn't a lie,
it's the truth.

594
00:40:14.169 --> 00:40:15.877
- Truly?
- Nope, a lie.

595
00:40:16.085 --> 00:40:17.085
A lie?

596
00:40:17.127 --> 00:40:18.127
I get it.

597
00:40:18.585 --> 00:40:20.919
Your culture forbids lying.

598
00:40:21.669 --> 00:40:23.189
But here, it's a whole different game.

599
00:40:27.752 --> 00:40:28.752
Umm,

600
00:40:29.377 --> 00:40:31.877
I know it's not like your airplane.

601
00:40:32.002 --> 00:40:33.002
It's a little different.

602
00:40:33.835 --> 00:40:34.915
Just adjust for a few days.

603
00:40:35.252 --> 00:40:37.752
And adjust to Mom's clothes for a bit too.

604
00:40:38.085 --> 00:40:40.353
We'll get you new clothes
first thing tomorrow.

605
00:40:43.419 --> 00:40:44.419
Tarika?

606
00:40:50.627 --> 00:40:52.267
She was here a second ago.
Where'd she go?

607
00:40:53.502 --> 00:40:54.544
Tarika!

608
00:41:01.210 --> 00:41:02.210
Tarika?

609
00:41:08.752 --> 00:41:09.794
Tarika... Tadaka!

610
00:41:11.294 --> 00:41:12.294
Tadaka!

611
00:41:14.710 --> 00:41:15.710
Tadaka!

612
00:41:23.127 --> 00:41:24.127
Shush.

613
00:41:25.252 --> 00:41:26.492
Why are you laughing like that?

614
00:41:27.127 --> 00:41:28.377
It's just how I laugh.

615
00:41:29.085 --> 00:41:30.085
Okay...

616
00:41:30.377 --> 00:41:31.857
But what are you doing under the bed?

617
00:41:36.752 --> 00:41:38.085
I like it here.

618
00:41:41.002 --> 00:41:42.544
Me too.

619
00:41:46.919 --> 00:41:48.502
I can hear your heart beat.

620
00:41:49.669 --> 00:41:50.794
It's racing.

621
00:41:52.002 --> 00:41:55.419
My heart always races when I'm with you.

622
00:42:14.794 --> 00:42:15.794
Alok!

623
00:42:16.710 --> 00:42:17.710
Alok!

624
00:42:20.460 --> 00:42:21.520
What are you doing down there?

625
00:42:21.544 --> 00:42:23.169
Mom, I was just...

626
00:42:25.710 --> 00:42:27.127
showing Tarika my room.

627
00:42:29.002 --> 00:42:29.936
Fine.

628
00:42:31.794 --> 00:42:33.544
Give her some milk once you're done.

629
00:42:34.210 --> 00:42:35.085
Hmm?

630
00:42:35.210 --> 00:42:36.210
Yes.

631
00:42:36.710 --> 00:42:37.710
Okay.

632
00:42:37.835 --> 00:42:39.210
My son's all grown up now.

633
00:42:40.210 --> 00:42:41.377
She loves him,

634
00:42:42.335 --> 00:42:43.710
she loves him not.

635
00:42:44.627 --> 00:42:45.835
She loves him,

636
00:42:47.169 --> 00:42:48.335
she loves him not.

637
00:42:55.835 --> 00:42:58.377
You're a Betaal and he's human...

638
00:43:00.169 --> 00:43:01.419
yet he still escaped?

639
00:43:02.585 --> 00:43:04.210
Shame on you, Veeran.

640
00:43:04.752 --> 00:43:07.044
I can't even show my teeth
to anyone now, thanks to you.

641
00:43:08.752 --> 00:43:10.585
I tried my best to stop him.

642
00:43:11.419 --> 00:43:13.502
But Tadaka ran away with that human.

643
00:43:14.002 --> 00:43:15.252
What now?

644
00:43:16.377 --> 00:43:17.377
I...

645
00:43:18.419 --> 00:43:19.419
I...

646
00:43:20.085 --> 00:43:22.794
- I...
- What's with all the "I... I... I..."?

647
00:43:24.585 --> 00:43:26.877
You'll keep whining
if you drink goat's blood.

648
00:43:27.794 --> 00:43:29.544
Start drinking human blood.

649
00:43:30.335 --> 00:43:32.294
We're forbidden from drinking human blood.

650
00:43:32.752 --> 00:43:35.710
What Tadaka did was also forbidden.

651
00:43:35.877 --> 00:43:36.877
What?

652
00:43:37.002 --> 00:43:38.044
She fell in love.

653
00:43:38.294 --> 00:43:40.002
- Love?
- Yes.

654
00:43:40.169 --> 00:43:43.502
That's why Tadaka saved
that human and ran away.

655
00:43:45.127 --> 00:43:48.502
That love will cause her
to make more mistakes in the future.

656
00:43:48.919 --> 00:43:50.252
So what are your orders?

657
00:43:50.710 --> 00:43:52.044
GO GET HIM BACK!!!

658
00:44:37.585 --> 00:44:38.585
Su... Sudha!

659
00:44:38.877 --> 00:44:39.749
Sudha!

660
00:44:39.750 --> 00:44:40.627
SUDHAAA!

661
00:44:41.835 --> 00:44:45.186
Tarika isn't a honey trap.

662
00:44:45.210 --> 00:44:46.252
What?

663
00:44:47.210 --> 00:44:48.877
She's paranormal.

664
00:44:49.669 --> 00:44:50.669
I know...

665
00:44:51.294 --> 00:44:52.520
she's normal.

666
00:44:52.544 --> 00:44:53.270
Hey...

667
00:44:53.294 --> 00:44:55.228
I know this will sound strange...

668
00:44:55.252 --> 00:44:57.085
Go on.

669
00:44:57.752 --> 00:45:00.919
She's possessed by a bat's spirit.

670
00:45:03.585 --> 00:45:04.353
Huh?

671
00:45:04.377 --> 00:45:05.877
A bat.

672
00:45:07.502 --> 00:45:10.002
I once got a wedding proposal
from a lawyer.

673
00:45:10.710 --> 00:45:12.002
He earned well too.

674
00:45:12.627 --> 00:45:14.252
But I chose you.

675
00:45:15.502 --> 00:45:18.710
Today, that lawyer's wife
must be sleeping peacefully.

676
00:45:19.210 --> 00:45:21.710
Come on Sudha, I'm not kidding.

677
00:45:21.835 --> 00:45:27.377
I just saw her jump
from Alok's window on to a tree.

678
00:45:28.210 --> 00:45:30.210
No human can do that.

679
00:45:30.377 --> 00:45:33.502
She's possessed by a bat!

680
00:45:35.169 --> 00:45:37.502
If I got possessed by a lioness,

681
00:45:38.294 --> 00:45:39.835
you'd be in deep trouble.

682
00:45:40.085 --> 00:45:41.460
Sudha, please, just hear me out.

683
00:45:42.919 --> 00:45:43.919
GO TO SLEEP!

684
00:45:48.252 --> 00:45:49.252
Good night.

685
00:46:14.794 --> 00:46:15.794
Tarika!

686
00:46:33.127 --> 00:46:34.585
Tadaka...
What are you doing?

687
00:46:39.419 --> 00:46:40.419
You were going to...

688
00:46:41.919 --> 00:46:43.002
Nope, not happening!

689
00:46:43.335 --> 00:46:44.169
You can't.

690
00:46:44.335 --> 00:46:45.085
I totally can.

691
00:46:45.210 --> 00:46:46.210
Quite easily, in fact.

692
00:46:46.752 --> 00:46:47.794
He's a dog!

693
00:46:48.085 --> 00:46:49.127
He's so cute...

694
00:46:49.585 --> 00:46:50.585
and chubby,

695
00:46:51.169 --> 00:46:53.020
just like a rabbit!

696
00:46:53.044 --> 00:46:54.127
Hand him over.

697
00:46:54.294 --> 00:46:55.353
Give me that dog.

698
00:46:55.377 --> 00:46:56.377
Come here, boy.

699
00:47:00.210 --> 00:47:01.960
He's really making you hungry, huh?

700
00:47:02.585 --> 00:47:03.585
Hmm.

701
00:47:04.419 --> 00:47:05.919
I'll sort you some food tomorrow.

702
00:47:06.294 --> 00:47:08.002
- Okay?
- Wait.

703
00:47:08.210 --> 00:47:09.020
Go away.

704
00:47:09.044 --> 00:47:10.044
Shoo!

705
00:47:13.960 --> 00:47:15.478
What, you'd eat a lizard too?

706
00:47:15.502 --> 00:47:16.502
Let's go.

707
00:47:25.794 --> 00:47:27.627
Sir, your car's crooked.

708
00:47:28.835 --> 00:47:31.585
Park it properly
or I'll file a complaint.

709
00:47:32.085 --> 00:47:33.127
Go on, do it.

710
00:47:34.127 --> 00:47:36.087
I'm running late, man.
Why are you messing around?

711
00:47:38.169 --> 00:47:41.085
Alok, we tore the place
apart looking for you that day.

712
00:47:41.627 --> 00:47:42.627
Thanks, bro.

713
00:47:42.835 --> 00:47:44.755
You two bolted
with your tails between your legs.

714
00:47:44.919 --> 00:47:45.853
Sorry, dude.

715
00:47:45.877 --> 00:47:47.478
Thank God Tarika saved me.
Otherwise I'd...

716
00:47:47.502 --> 00:47:49.960
Wait, Tarika? That mountain girl?

717
00:47:50.294 --> 00:47:51.311
How do you even know about her?

718
00:47:51.335 --> 00:47:52.935
The whole group won't shut up about her.

719
00:47:52.960 --> 00:47:54.002
So, what's she like?

720
00:47:54.710 --> 00:47:56.460
I don't think she's all that beautiful.

721
00:48:12.460 --> 00:48:14.180
By the way, you look really pretty tonight.

722
00:48:14.502 --> 00:48:16.627
What am I doing here dressed like this?

723
00:48:17.502 --> 00:48:18.502
It's our first date.

724
00:48:18.877 --> 00:48:20.377
I wanted it to be a bit special.

725
00:48:21.085 --> 00:48:22.335
Spe...

726
00:48:22.585 --> 00:48:23.960
It's a top-notch place.

727
00:48:24.377 --> 00:48:26.419
They've got great selection of meat here.

728
00:48:26.835 --> 00:48:31.460
- I'm not bad at heart,
- Disgusting!

729
00:48:31.627 --> 00:48:36.169
I have just one fault I confess.

730
00:48:36.960 --> 00:48:40.919
Not out of habit,

731
00:48:41.460 --> 00:48:45.978
I drink for the thirst, no less.

732
00:48:53.169 --> 00:48:58.085
So tell me, what happens to the
drink-bearers when my cup stops brinking?

733
00:49:01.169 --> 00:49:05.335
So tell me, what happens to the
drink-bearers when my cup stops brinking?

734
00:49:05.585 --> 00:49:09.270
So tell me, what happens to the
drink-bearers when my cup stops brinking?

735
00:49:09.294 --> 00:49:13.835
I'd rather stop living than stop drinking.

736
00:49:21.502 --> 00:49:29.311
If I had to count the glasses that
I keep downing, I'd rather stop counting,

737
00:49:29.335 --> 00:49:33.311
I'd rather stop living than stop drinking.

738
00:49:33.335 --> 00:49:35.770
- Your eyes...
- Poison, baby.

739
00:49:35.794 --> 00:49:37.978
- Your words...
- Poison, baby.

740
00:49:38.002 --> 00:49:41.478
Your attitude is delicious,

741
00:49:41.502 --> 00:49:43.770
- Your moves...
- Poison, baby.

742
00:49:43.794 --> 00:49:46.020
- The way you groove...
- Poison, baby.

743
00:49:46.044 --> 00:49:49.794
Even your atrocity is precious.

744
00:49:57.502 --> 00:50:01.770
As soon as I took a sip of the drink,

745
00:50:01.794 --> 00:50:06.127
I felt younger, years gone in a blink.

746
00:50:09.835 --> 00:50:13.728
With a glass in hand
there's nothing I won't do,

747
00:50:13.752 --> 00:50:19.478
All the things without that drink
I couldn't pull through.

748
00:50:19.502 --> 00:50:27.270
I'd crack a bottle on the head of anyone
who's prying,

749
00:50:27.294 --> 00:50:32.085
I'd rather stop living
than stop my drinking.

750
00:50:35.544 --> 00:50:43.311
So tell me, what happens to the
drink-bearers when my cup stops brinking?

751
00:50:43.335 --> 00:50:47.228
I'd rather stop living than stop drinking.

752
00:50:47.252 --> 00:50:49.728
- Your eyes...
- Poison, baby.

753
00:50:49.752 --> 00:50:51.936
- Your words...
- Poison, baby.

754
00:50:51.960 --> 00:50:55.520
Your attitude is delicious,

755
00:50:55.544 --> 00:50:57.770
- Your moves...
- Poison, baby.

756
00:50:57.794 --> 00:51:00.020
- The way you groove...
- Poison, baby.

757
00:51:00.044 --> 00:51:03.877
Even your atrocity is precious.

758
00:51:04.794 --> 00:51:06.335
Poison, baby.

759
00:51:06.835 --> 00:51:08.127
Poison, baby.

760
00:51:12.835 --> 00:51:14.210
Poison, baby.

761
00:51:14.835 --> 00:51:17.710
Poison... baby.

762
00:51:21.794 --> 00:51:22.954
What the hell was that about?

763
00:51:23.252 --> 00:51:24.252
We're in Delhi.

764
00:51:24.627 --> 00:51:26.061
Here, even eye contact
is taken out of context.

765
00:51:26.085 --> 00:51:27.460
Guys think a girl's easy.

766
00:51:28.294 --> 00:51:30.752
I don't know what came over me.

767
00:51:31.210 --> 00:51:32.544
My head was spinning.

768
00:51:33.127 --> 00:51:34.710
You don't drink often?

769
00:51:34.919 --> 00:51:36.002
Never had it before.

770
00:51:36.252 --> 00:51:37.252
That's why.

771
00:51:37.419 --> 00:51:39.960
Let's head home.
I'll make you some lemonade, sober you up.

772
00:51:42.627 --> 00:51:43.436
Stop the car!

773
00:51:43.460 --> 00:51:45.085
Stop! Stop the car!

774
00:51:47.335 --> 00:51:48.335
Stop!

775
00:51:49.919 --> 00:51:51.794
Use blinkers, man. Use blinkers!

776
00:51:53.460 --> 00:51:54.752
Overtake them.

777
00:51:54.877 --> 00:51:56.186
Step on it! Step on it!
Come on, step on it!

778
00:51:56.210 --> 00:51:57.728
How dare you!

779
00:51:57.752 --> 00:51:59.686
Where are you taking your sister-in-law?

780
00:51:59.710 --> 00:52:01.436
STOP THE CAR!

781
00:52:01.460 --> 00:52:03.502
- Stop the car!
- Let us have some fun too.

782
00:52:04.627 --> 00:52:05.811
Why are they following us?

783
00:52:05.835 --> 00:52:07.811
- Where are you taking your sister-in-law?
- Stop the car!

784
00:52:07.835 --> 00:52:09.002
I need to lose them.

785
00:52:09.919 --> 00:52:10.919
Shit.

786
00:52:11.960 --> 00:52:12.936
Hey sweetheart!

787
00:52:12.960 --> 00:52:14.103
Don't you get it?!

788
00:52:14.127 --> 00:52:15.645
Follow him... go after him!

789
00:52:15.669 --> 00:52:17.145
- Overtake him... overtake him!
- Follow him... go after him!

790
00:52:17.169 --> 00:52:18.585
Step on it! Step on it!

791
00:52:24.252 --> 00:52:25.502
Shit. Shit. Shit.

792
00:52:31.502 --> 00:52:33.127
Where will you go now?

793
00:52:33.460 --> 00:52:34.919
Come on out, kiddo...

794
00:52:35.419 --> 00:52:37.085
- Jimmy's waiting for you.
- Come on out.

795
00:52:37.210 --> 00:52:38.502
Stay in the car.

796
00:52:38.627 --> 00:52:39.627
I'll handle this.

797
00:52:40.085 --> 00:52:40.999
Okay?

798
00:52:41.000 --> 00:52:42.645
Come on out, ma'am. We won't hurt you.

799
00:52:42.669 --> 00:52:43.794
Come to daddy, kiddo.

800
00:52:47.002 --> 00:52:49.169
Scared already?

801
00:52:49.960 --> 00:52:50.686
Hey, kiddo!

802
00:52:50.710 --> 00:52:53.294
Why do all girls go
for clean-shaven losers?

803
00:52:53.419 --> 00:52:54.669
We can clean up too, bro.

804
00:52:57.419 --> 00:52:58.460
Hey baby-steps...

805
00:52:58.877 --> 00:53:00.710
Hey baby-steps... hurry up already!

806
00:53:01.294 --> 00:53:02.374
I don't have time to waste.

807
00:53:02.669 --> 00:53:03.669
Move faster!

808
00:53:04.169 --> 00:53:05.395
Let's talk, bro.

809
00:53:05.419 --> 00:53:06.710
You're in big trouble.

810
00:53:07.169 --> 00:53:07.978
Shut it.

811
00:53:08.002 --> 00:53:09.353
- Let's talk.
- Let's talk?

812
00:53:09.377 --> 00:53:10.165
Yeah.

813
00:53:10.166 --> 00:53:11.544
She's a nice girl.

814
00:53:12.044 --> 00:53:13.603
Why chase her if she isn't interested?

815
00:53:13.627 --> 00:53:14.627
She is interested.

816
00:53:14.752 --> 00:53:15.952
Who was she with at the party?

817
00:53:16.127 --> 00:53:17.127
Jimmy.

818
00:53:17.460 --> 00:53:18.580
So why'd she leave with you?

819
00:53:18.710 --> 00:53:19.752
That's cheating, dude.

820
00:53:20.085 --> 00:53:21.728
Wait here.
These kids will look after you.

821
00:53:21.752 --> 00:53:22.752
I'll handle her.

822
00:53:22.919 --> 00:53:23.919
Let it go, bro.

823
00:53:24.044 --> 00:53:25.645
Just take some cash and sort it out.

824
00:53:25.669 --> 00:53:26.877
I can pay you.

825
00:53:27.085 --> 00:53:28.395
I don't want trouble, bro.

826
00:53:28.419 --> 00:53:29.395
He'll pay us, he says!

827
00:53:29.419 --> 00:53:30.699
I don't want any trouble either,

828
00:53:32.085 --> 00:53:33.127
I want something else.

829
00:53:36.960 --> 00:53:38.811
Cigarette smoking is injurious to...

830
00:54:01.544 --> 00:54:02.270
Go fetch your sister-in-law.

831
00:54:02.294 --> 00:54:04.627
Be nice. Tell her Jimmy's calling her.

832
00:56:21.502 --> 00:56:22.202
Tadaka!!!

833
00:56:26.627 --> 00:56:27.919
Wh... what are you doing?

834
00:56:44.377 --> 00:56:45.752
Let's get out of here. Hurry up!

835
00:57:03.169 --> 00:57:04.169
Alright, now tell me...

836
00:57:04.627 --> 00:57:05.835
That.. What was that?

837
00:57:06.544 --> 00:57:07.584
What were you going to do?

838
00:57:07.627 --> 00:57:09.307
Speak up... why are you so quiet now, huh?

839
00:57:10.835 --> 00:57:12.978
- You're... a man-eater?
- No, no way.

840
00:57:13.002 --> 00:57:14.460
No! Stay back! One arm distance!

841
00:57:15.794 --> 00:57:16.853
I'm not a man-eater.

842
00:57:16.877 --> 00:57:17.645
Then?

843
00:57:17.669 --> 00:57:18.811
I wasn't going to eat him.

844
00:57:18.835 --> 00:57:19.686
Then?

845
00:57:19.710 --> 00:57:21.311
I was going to drink his blood.

846
00:57:21.335 --> 00:57:22.877
BLOODDDD?

847
00:57:25.669 --> 00:57:27.029
You were going to drink his blood?

848
00:57:27.502 --> 00:57:29.502
I'd never make such a mistake.

849
00:57:29.960 --> 00:57:32.210
But when they started hitting you,

850
00:57:32.919 --> 00:57:35.085
I don't know what came over me...

851
00:57:35.710 --> 00:57:37.669
I lost control.

852
00:57:38.252 --> 00:57:39.252
But... blood?!

853
00:57:41.960 --> 00:57:43.085
Do you really drink blood?

854
00:57:43.794 --> 00:57:45.710
Yes, I drink blood.

855
00:57:46.835 --> 00:57:48.544
That's a weird habit.

856
00:57:48.978 --> 00:57:50.745
There are so many drinks in the world,
yet you choose blood!

857
00:57:50.769 --> 00:57:51.769
Why are you doing this?

858
00:57:51.960 --> 00:57:53.186
- Alok...
- No, no, no, stay back.

859
00:57:53.210 --> 00:57:54.978
You relishing a barasingha
is still something I can relate to.

860
00:57:55.002 --> 00:57:56.502
People have exotic taste buds.

861
00:57:56.669 --> 00:57:57.669
They eat anything...

862
00:57:58.002 --> 00:57:59.686
dogs, cats, jackal or even bats.

863
00:57:59.710 --> 00:58:01.419
But who drink blood, dude?!

864
00:58:01.835 --> 00:58:02.835
Alok...

865
00:58:03.752 --> 00:58:06.377
Wait a second... Are you a vampire?

866
00:58:06.669 --> 00:58:07.669
Vampire?

867
00:58:07.877 --> 00:58:09.811
Like in those horror movies?

868
00:58:09.835 --> 00:58:11.085
They drink blood,

869
00:58:11.335 --> 00:58:14.020
get burned by sunlight, sleep in coffins,
and have no shadows.

870
00:58:14.044 --> 00:58:15.044
Close cousins of ghosts?

871
00:58:15.502 --> 00:58:16.794
Invisible in mirrors.

872
00:58:19.835 --> 00:58:20.835
I can see you.

873
00:58:20.960 --> 00:58:22.645
- Are you a hybrid?
- Alok...

874
00:58:22.669 --> 00:58:24.109
- Stop right there.
- We are Betaals.

875
00:58:24.794 --> 00:58:25.877
We are Betaals.

876
00:58:26.210 --> 00:58:28.228
We only drink blood.

877
00:58:28.252 --> 00:58:29.627
"We ONLY drink blood."

878
00:58:29.794 --> 00:58:30.794
What a claim!

879
00:58:31.127 --> 00:58:31.936
- Alok...
- No!

880
00:58:31.960 --> 00:58:33.320
Don't come closer, I'll smash you.

881
00:58:34.960 --> 00:58:37.280
How would I even explain
to the world who and what you are?

882
00:58:37.794 --> 00:58:40.020
Tomorrow at dinner when Mom asks
what Tarika wants... what will I say?

883
00:58:40.044 --> 00:58:41.884
"Nothing, Mom,
just give her some fresh blood!"

884
00:58:42.377 --> 00:58:43.811
Only the veteran actor Dharmendra
has the right to say,

885
00:58:43.835 --> 00:58:45.585
"I'll drink your blood, you dog."

886
00:58:46.085 --> 00:58:48.460
He too just says it,
never actually drinks it.

887
00:58:51.377 --> 00:58:52.377
SHIT!!!

888
00:58:52.835 --> 00:58:54.355
Here I thought you were a Wonder Girl,

889
00:58:54.627 --> 00:58:55.794
turns out you're Dracula.

890
00:58:56.210 --> 00:58:57.210
Dracula?

891
00:58:57.544 --> 00:58:58.544
Who's that?

892
00:58:58.627 --> 00:58:59.728
You don't know who Dracula is?

893
00:58:59.752 --> 00:59:03.544
Collar up, fangs out, walks like this.

894
00:59:03.752 --> 00:59:06.169
I mean...
He's got to be related to you somehow.

895
00:59:06.377 --> 00:59:08.585
You might not know him.
Maybe he's one of your uncles.

896
00:59:09.252 --> 00:59:12.919
Alok, we don't drink human blood anymore.

897
00:59:13.419 --> 00:59:14.502
Why should I believe you?

898
00:59:15.210 --> 00:59:15.919
Why?

899
00:59:16.044 --> 00:59:17.794
Isn't it enough that I said we don't?

900
00:59:19.252 --> 00:59:20.252
I don't know.

901
00:59:20.919 --> 00:59:23.169
We used to drink human blood...

902
00:59:23.960 --> 00:59:26.835
but only of those less human, more beasts.

903
00:59:28.419 --> 00:59:32.669
But after 1947, things changed.

904
00:59:34.085 --> 00:59:35.085
What do you mean?

905
00:59:43.544 --> 00:59:44.919
Riots broke out.

906
00:59:45.960 --> 00:59:49.002
Rioters were rolling into town,
packed into trains.

907
00:59:54.752 --> 01:00:00.002
We went there to drink the killers' blood
and save the innocent.

908
01:00:03.335 --> 01:00:06.752
But when we arrived, we were stunned.

909
01:00:07.919 --> 01:00:10.585
There weren't rioters,
just innocent people

910
01:00:11.252 --> 01:00:14.585
who'd slaughtered each other,
and were lying dead.

911
01:00:15.294 --> 01:00:19.835
We'd never seen that much blood.

912
01:00:20.835 --> 01:00:27.210
No other animal kills like that
for no reason.

913
01:00:28.669 --> 01:00:30.960
From that day, we decided

914
01:00:31.835 --> 01:00:33.752
humans are poisonous

915
01:00:35.252 --> 01:00:37.585
because their blood is toxic.

916
01:00:38.460 --> 01:00:40.752
So we stopped drinking their blood.

917
01:00:53.294 --> 01:00:54.377
You are lying.

918
01:00:55.044 --> 01:00:56.877
Back in that cave, that poet...

919
01:00:57.585 --> 01:00:58.710
he wanted to drink my blood.

920
01:00:59.210 --> 01:01:03.002
That's why we locked him
in the cursed mountain.

921
01:01:03.794 --> 01:01:04.794
Who is he?

922
01:01:05.585 --> 01:01:07.127
The most powerful,

923
01:01:07.627 --> 01:01:08.960
deadliest of us all...

924
01:01:09.585 --> 01:01:10.585
Yakshashan.

925
01:01:11.377 --> 01:01:13.585
Our ancestor.

926
01:01:15.252 --> 01:01:17.794
The one who made us Betaals.

927
01:01:18.835 --> 01:01:19.919
Our hero...

928
01:01:21.169 --> 01:01:22.169
our Thamma.

929
01:01:25.585 --> 01:01:28.919
We all agreed not to drink human blood,

930
01:01:30.835 --> 01:01:33.585
but Yakshashan refused.

931
01:01:43.377 --> 01:01:44.585
You broke the rule.

932
01:01:45.544 --> 01:01:46.669
You will be punished.

933
01:01:49.294 --> 01:01:50.377
Your rules are baseless.

934
01:01:50.919 --> 01:01:52.919
Drinking human blood is in our nature.

935
01:01:53.585 --> 01:01:56.645
One day, we'll turn them all
and rule the world.

936
01:01:56.669 --> 01:01:57.669
We will rule!

937
01:01:57.877 --> 01:02:01.710
We want to break free
from this curse of drinking blood.

938
01:02:03.335 --> 01:02:04.585
You're our ancestor.

939
01:02:05.794 --> 01:02:06.936
You created us.

940
01:02:06.960 --> 01:02:10.853
That's why we keep offering
animal sacrifices to keep you alive.

941
01:02:10.877 --> 01:02:12.627
From now on,

942
01:02:13.585 --> 01:02:16.228
you'll stay imprisoned in this cave.

943
01:02:16.252 --> 01:02:17.978
For how long do you think
you can keep me imprisoned?

944
01:02:18.002 --> 01:02:19.186
Hundred years of toil and pain,

945
01:02:19.210 --> 01:02:21.770
The day one of you breaks the rule

946
01:02:21.794 --> 01:02:23.561
and turns a human into a Betaal...

947
01:02:23.585 --> 01:02:25.853
I'll be free.

948
01:02:25.877 --> 01:02:27.627
FREE!!!

949
01:02:28.419 --> 01:02:30.335
FREE!!!

950
01:02:32.544 --> 01:02:35.794
You said you imprisoned Yakshashan
after the 1947 incident.

951
01:02:37.585 --> 01:02:38.585
You were there?

952
01:02:40.127 --> 01:02:41.377
I mean... How?

953
01:02:45.627 --> 01:02:46.835
I'm not human.

954
01:02:48.335 --> 01:02:50.252
I don't have a heartbeat.

955
01:02:54.460 --> 01:02:56.544
But you do.

956
01:02:59.085 --> 01:03:02.127
And that's what pulls me to you.

957
01:03:04.919 --> 01:03:06.460
It just... compels me.

958
01:03:17.252 --> 01:03:18.252
Who are you?

959
01:03:18.669 --> 01:03:19.835
Inspector P.K. Yadav.

960
01:03:20.585 --> 01:03:21.669
Oh. Goyal.

961
01:03:26.002 --> 01:03:27.002
Hello.

962
01:03:28.544 --> 01:03:30.294
All good, Officer?

963
01:03:32.127 --> 01:03:33.561
No Mr. Goyal,
I'm afraid things aren't looking good.

964
01:03:33.585 --> 01:03:35.585
Oh, so you are here seeking a donation?

965
01:03:36.502 --> 01:03:38.502
Do I look like the one
who'd seek a donation?

966
01:03:40.085 --> 01:03:41.835
I'm here to investigate.

967
01:03:42.294 --> 01:03:43.294
Investigate what?

968
01:03:43.460 --> 01:03:45.169
Something happened with a couple of boys.

969
01:03:47.669 --> 01:03:48.869
Do you know anything about it?

970
01:03:49.252 --> 01:03:50.252
No.

971
01:03:50.669 --> 01:03:52.169
If I did, I'd tell you.

972
01:03:52.919 --> 01:03:54.335
I'd do anything for the police.

973
01:03:54.710 --> 01:03:55.710
- Really?
- Yeah.

974
01:03:55.960 --> 01:03:57.520
Okay, so what have you done
for the police?

975
01:03:57.544 --> 01:03:59.002
I've watched Singham eight times.

976
01:03:59.544 --> 01:04:00.544
Big fan.

977
01:04:01.044 --> 01:04:02.044
Big fan, sir.

978
01:04:20.835 --> 01:04:21.835
What's your name?

979
01:04:23.252 --> 01:04:23.952
Tarika.

980
01:04:24.127 --> 01:04:25.127
Tadaka.

981
01:04:29.044 --> 01:04:30.544
Tadaka or Tarika?

982
01:04:31.377 --> 01:04:32.377
Only Tarika.

983
01:04:34.877 --> 01:04:37.919
So, Ms. "Only Tarika,"
were you at a party earlier?

984
01:04:39.710 --> 01:04:41.020
- Hmm?
- Yes.

985
01:04:41.044 --> 01:04:42.169
Hmm.

986
01:04:42.794 --> 01:04:44.669
Did some guys misbehave with you there?

987
01:04:45.210 --> 01:04:46.335
Did they cause trouble?

988
01:04:46.960 --> 01:04:50.252
That's what I want to discuss...
in private.

989
01:04:51.919 --> 01:04:52.919
Let's go.

990
01:05:08.835 --> 01:05:10.395
Rakhtrambha!

991
01:05:10.419 --> 01:05:12.960
Sasakhtrambha!

992
01:05:16.544 --> 01:05:17.544
You...?!

993
01:05:17.752 --> 01:05:18.752
You too?

994
01:05:19.919 --> 01:05:20.919
Me too.

995
01:05:22.502 --> 01:05:23.502
Knew it...

996
01:05:24.794 --> 01:05:27.877
knew who you were the second
I saw those guys.

997
01:05:31.627 --> 01:05:32.710
Why did you kill them?

998
01:05:33.877 --> 01:05:34.877
Kill them?

999
01:05:38.044 --> 01:05:39.169
You killed them, right?

1000
01:05:39.877 --> 01:05:40.877
Hmm?

1001
01:05:44.960 --> 01:05:47.044
Good thing you just broke their necks.

1002
01:05:48.419 --> 01:05:52.460
Biting them and drinking blood
would've been caused a lot of trouble.

1003
01:05:53.335 --> 01:05:54.377
Where did you come from?

1004
01:05:54.710 --> 01:05:56.169
Why did you kill them?

1005
01:05:56.502 --> 01:05:57.502
They...

1006
01:05:57.919 --> 01:06:00.835
they were hurting Alok.

1007
01:06:01.877 --> 01:06:03.252
My head was spinning.

1008
01:06:04.210 --> 01:06:06.669
I lost control.

1009
01:06:07.460 --> 01:06:10.835
I can't remember what happened next.

1010
01:06:11.877 --> 01:06:14.794
For 172 years,
it has been my responsibility,

1011
01:06:15.419 --> 01:06:18.210
to maintain the equilibrium
between humans and our kind.

1012
01:06:19.460 --> 01:06:22.210
And you're messing up that balance.

1013
01:06:23.085 --> 01:06:25.585
Alok's making you lose control.

1014
01:06:26.335 --> 01:06:29.210
You could hurt him and his family.

1015
01:06:29.710 --> 01:06:32.460
You could attack them,
bite them, drink their blood.

1016
01:06:32.835 --> 01:06:35.585
You should leave
before you cause more trouble.

1017
01:06:36.960 --> 01:06:37.811
GO.

1018
01:06:45.169 --> 01:06:46.169
Congratulations, son.

1019
01:06:46.419 --> 01:06:47.419
She finally got caught.

1020
01:06:47.669 --> 01:06:48.770
Come on, Dad.

1021
01:06:50.669 --> 01:06:51.669
All okay, dear?

1022
01:06:52.210 --> 01:06:53.210
Tarika?

1023
01:06:53.419 --> 01:06:54.835
So... what happened?

1024
01:06:58.877 --> 01:07:00.169
Why aren't you saying anything?

1025
01:07:00.585 --> 01:07:01.877
I have to leave, Alok.

1026
01:07:02.210 --> 01:07:03.270
What did the officer say?

1027
01:07:03.294 --> 01:07:05.014
Don't worry, whatever it is,
I'll handle it.

1028
01:07:05.294 --> 01:07:08.919
He knows what I did to those guys.

1029
01:07:09.377 --> 01:07:11.057
What did you do?
What exactly does he know?

1030
01:07:11.752 --> 01:07:14.210
The police found their bodies.

1031
01:07:14.877 --> 01:07:16.085
Did you kill them?

1032
01:07:16.544 --> 01:07:17.544
I don't know.

1033
01:07:17.835 --> 01:07:19.311
What do you mean by "you don't know"?

1034
01:07:19.335 --> 01:07:23.186
All I know is you might be
in danger because of me.

1035
01:07:23.210 --> 01:07:24.353
You said you don't drink human blood...

1036
01:07:24.377 --> 01:07:25.919
I'm a Betaal, Alok!

1037
01:07:26.752 --> 01:07:31.502
What if I lose control one day
and hurt you?

1038
01:07:45.044 --> 01:07:48.919
Whether or not I am there with you.

1039
01:07:51.127 --> 01:07:53.044
I want to be with you...

1040
01:07:55.585 --> 01:07:57.335
but I just can't.

1041
01:08:01.169 --> 01:08:03.252
Our worlds are too different.

1042
01:08:06.585 --> 01:08:08.561
- I have to go.
- Please, don't leave.

1043
01:08:31.044 --> 01:08:35.270
What more could I want than you

1044
01:08:35.294 --> 01:08:43.294
remembering me your whole life through,

1045
01:08:44.752 --> 01:08:49.710
Whether or not I am there with you.

1046
01:08:49.835 --> 01:08:54.252
Whether or not I am there with you.

1047
01:08:54.544 --> 01:08:58.728
Even without being beside you,

1048
01:08:58.752 --> 01:09:06.752
Each day, each moment,
I'll still be with you,

1049
01:09:08.335 --> 01:09:12.960
Whether or not I am there with you.

1050
01:09:13.127 --> 01:09:17.145
Whether or not I am there with you.

1051
01:09:17.169 --> 01:09:21.460
I am not away from you,

1052
01:09:22.002 --> 01:09:26.561
I'm right there where you are too.

1053
01:09:26.585 --> 01:09:31.127
I am not away from you,

1054
01:09:31.419 --> 01:09:35.794
I'm right there where you are too.

1055
01:09:45.919 --> 01:09:50.252
I'll always flourish in you,

1056
01:09:50.877 --> 01:09:58.877
Whether or not I am there with you.

1057
01:10:27.085 --> 01:10:29.002
Tarika, please don't go.

1058
01:10:29.835 --> 01:10:31.127
I don't want to lose you.

1059
01:10:31.585 --> 01:10:33.002
Tarika, please stay.

1060
01:10:34.627 --> 01:10:35.794
Please don't go.

1061
01:10:38.210 --> 01:10:39.294
Stop the bus.

1062
01:11:17.502 --> 01:11:19.770
Alok!

1063
01:11:24.377 --> 01:11:25.377
Alok!

1064
01:11:30.419 --> 01:11:34.353
What more could I want than you

1065
01:11:34.377 --> 01:11:42.377
- remembering me your whole life through,
- Alok...

1066
01:11:45.044 --> 01:11:50.520
Whether or not I am there with you.

1067
01:11:50.544 --> 01:11:54.811
Whether or not I am there with you.

1068
01:11:54.835 --> 01:11:58.794
Whether or not I am there with you.

1069
01:12:03.389 --> 01:12:04.389
Quick! Quick! Right!

1070
01:12:07.681 --> 01:12:09.121
Sorry, ma'am, you can't come inside.

1071
01:12:25.514 --> 01:12:27.032
This way. Tarika!

1072
01:12:27.056 --> 01:12:28.056
Tarika!

1073
01:12:28.389 --> 01:12:29.990
Where is Alok?

1074
01:12:30.014 --> 01:12:31.556
WHERE IS ALOK?!!!

1075
01:12:49.181 --> 01:12:51.139
Doctor, Alok...?

1076
01:12:53.056 --> 01:12:54.056
I'm sorry.

1077
01:13:03.556 --> 01:13:04.931
Sudha...

1078
01:14:32.848 --> 01:14:35.306
FREEDOOM!

1079
01:14:40.056 --> 01:14:41.348
The patient's not in the room.

1080
01:14:41.598 --> 01:14:42.598
He's not?

1081
01:14:45.056 --> 01:14:46.056
Alok...?

1082
01:14:51.264 --> 01:14:52.348
Alok!

1083
01:14:54.431 --> 01:14:55.889
Where's Alok?

1084
01:15:04.806 --> 01:15:05.806
Alok!

1085
01:16:21.889 --> 01:16:23.014
ALOKKK!!!

1086
01:16:25.681 --> 01:16:26.681
What's wrong?

1087
01:16:27.014 --> 01:16:28.098
Are you alright?

1088
01:16:32.348 --> 01:16:33.348
Aa...

1089
01:16:33.514 --> 01:16:36.014
- Where's Alok?
- He's fine, Alok is fine.

1090
01:16:36.139 --> 01:16:37.782
He's been discharged.
He's sleeping in his room.

1091
01:16:37.806 --> 01:16:40.490
I saw him at the hospital.

1092
01:16:40.514 --> 01:16:42.806
Good you found him.

1093
01:16:43.223 --> 01:16:47.264
Alok woke up and somehow
went upstairs by mistake.

1094
01:16:47.764 --> 01:16:48.865
He got upstairs by mistake?

1095
01:16:48.889 --> 01:16:49.598
Yes.

1096
01:16:49.848 --> 01:16:51.365
Then he ended up
in the blood bank by mistake?

1097
01:16:51.389 --> 01:16:52.115
Yes.

1098
01:16:52.139 --> 01:16:54.181
Who makes such detailed mistakes, huh?

1099
01:16:54.764 --> 01:16:55.907
What about the teeth?

1100
01:16:55.931 --> 01:16:57.514
- What teeth?
- Alok's teeth!

1101
01:16:57.639 --> 01:16:59.032
Which teeth? Whose teeth? What...

1102
01:16:59.056 --> 01:17:01.074
He tried to attack his own father!

1103
01:17:01.098 --> 01:17:01.798
Huh?

1104
01:17:02.889 --> 01:17:04.389
The doctor said

1105
01:17:04.681 --> 01:17:07.264
you might be delusional after
your head injury

1106
01:17:07.473 --> 01:17:09.056
and say strange things.

1107
01:17:09.931 --> 01:17:10.973
You should rest.

1108
01:17:11.723 --> 01:17:13.003
There's nothing to be afraid of.

1109
01:18:03.431 --> 01:18:04.681
Tadaka, what's wrong with me?

1110
01:18:05.264 --> 01:18:06.549
I acted strangely
at the hospital yesterday.

1111
01:18:06.573 --> 01:18:07.574
Today, I feel weird.

1112
01:18:07.598 --> 01:18:10.431
I can't feel my pulse or heartbeat.

1113
01:18:16.473 --> 01:18:18.240
Rakhtrambha!

1114
01:18:18.264 --> 01:18:20.889
Sasakhtrambha!

1115
01:18:27.098 --> 01:18:28.098
Huh?

1116
01:18:54.264 --> 01:18:56.681
You turned me?

1117
01:18:58.473 --> 01:18:59.473
So I'm dead now?

1118
01:19:00.639 --> 01:19:01.723
I'm not human anymore?

1119
01:19:03.598 --> 01:19:04.598
Shit!

1120
01:19:04.931 --> 01:19:06.449
Shit! Shit! Shit!

1121
01:19:06.473 --> 01:19:07.282
What do I even do now?

1122
01:19:07.306 --> 01:19:10.181
My life, dreams, ambitions...
it's all over now.

1123
01:19:10.348 --> 01:19:12.181
How do I even face social media?

1124
01:19:12.806 --> 01:19:15.282
How will I ever enjoy Rajma-chawal
again?

1125
01:19:15.306 --> 01:19:17.556
Guess there goes my life insurance too.

1126
01:19:18.181 --> 01:19:19.157
Why did you do this?

1127
01:19:19.181 --> 01:19:21.365
You would be dead if I didn't, Alok.

1128
01:19:21.389 --> 01:19:25.639
Killing me and then saying I would
be dead otherwise makes zero sense!

1129
01:19:25.973 --> 01:19:27.365
You were so quick to preach back then...

1130
01:19:27.389 --> 01:19:29.157
Humans are this, humans are that.

1131
01:19:29.181 --> 01:19:30.657
They have hatred in their blood.

1132
01:19:30.681 --> 01:19:31.740
Humans are poisonous.

1133
01:19:31.764 --> 01:19:32.907
They are like cloves, garlic and what not.

1134
01:19:32.931 --> 01:19:34.907
What was that about?
And what about your rules?

1135
01:19:34.931 --> 01:19:36.907
You said you cannot bite humans.

1136
01:19:36.931 --> 01:19:38.973
So why did you bite me?

1137
01:19:52.431 --> 01:19:55.348
Whether or not I am there with you.

1138
01:19:55.514 --> 01:19:57.389
You were dying, Alok...

1139
01:19:58.139 --> 01:20:00.098
I didn't want to lose you.

1140
01:20:03.973 --> 01:20:08.990
Love that no one can understand but you,

1141
01:20:09.014 --> 01:20:13.574
Something that's only felt by through you.

1142
01:20:13.598 --> 01:20:18.365
Something that cannot
be measured or subdued,

1143
01:20:18.389 --> 01:20:23.032
Something that even time
can't hold from you.

1144
01:20:23.056 --> 01:20:27.324
I am not away from you,

1145
01:20:27.348 --> 01:20:32.014
I'm right there where you are too.

1146
01:20:32.723 --> 01:20:37.764
Now I am free of them too,

1147
01:20:38.181 --> 01:20:41.324
Whether or not I am there with you.

1148
01:20:41.348 --> 01:20:44.223
If not as a human, then as a Betaal...

1149
01:20:44.931 --> 01:20:47.514
I just wanted to stay with you, Alok.

1150
01:20:48.931 --> 01:20:51.306
Even if it was just
for a little while longer.

1151
01:20:52.556 --> 01:20:53.973
Why just a little longer?

1152
01:20:54.931 --> 01:20:58.389
Now I want to be
with you forever and ever and ever.

1153
01:21:01.223 --> 01:21:05.723
By the way, even dying a hundred
times for this kiss is totally worth it.

1154
01:21:06.306 --> 01:21:10.990
Whether or not I am there with you.

1155
01:21:11.014 --> 01:21:13.389
With you...

1156
01:21:13.931 --> 01:21:17.723
Like a bird,
I wish to fly through the boundless sky,

1157
01:21:17.848 --> 01:21:21.699
Today I'm free in the garden
where the world lies.

1158
01:21:21.723 --> 01:21:23.824
Like a bird, I wish to fly...

1159
01:21:25.348 --> 01:21:26.282
We've got good news!

1160
01:21:27.431 --> 01:21:31.264
How about treating me to the blood
of a diabetic as something sweet?

1161
01:21:31.639 --> 01:21:33.598
It's been ages since such fires were lit.

1162
01:21:34.306 --> 01:21:37.973
Tadaka bit that human
and turned him into a Betaal!

1163
01:21:39.306 --> 01:21:40.115
But Yakshasan...

1164
01:21:40.139 --> 01:21:41.598
No ifs or buts!

1165
01:21:42.556 --> 01:21:44.740
Your Thamma will be free...

1166
01:21:44.764 --> 01:21:47.848
And Tadaka will be locked away here.

1167
01:21:51.473 --> 01:21:53.556
What's eating you, Rakhtash?

1168
01:21:54.806 --> 01:21:56.973
The king of kings is back.

1169
01:21:57.098 --> 01:21:58.818
Aren't you going to give me
a grand welcome?

1170
01:21:59.348 --> 01:22:00.824
Hurry up and make arrangements.

1171
01:22:00.848 --> 01:22:02.889
I'll get warmed up...

1172
01:22:03.889 --> 01:22:06.949
After all, soon I'll rule...
the world!

1173
01:22:09.014 --> 01:22:12.699
Like a bird,
I wish to fly through the boundless sky,

1174
01:22:12.723 --> 01:22:16.181
Today I'm free in the garden
where the world lies.

1175
01:22:18.181 --> 01:22:20.115
I've broken the cardinal rule,

1176
01:22:20.139 --> 01:22:23.181
and that could set Yakshasan free.

1177
01:22:23.639 --> 01:22:25.282
Who knows what he'll do then?

1178
01:22:25.306 --> 01:22:27.223
He'll drink human blood, obviously.

1179
01:22:27.723 --> 01:22:30.723
Tell me something, you Betaals...

1180
01:22:31.556 --> 01:22:35.764
Sorry... "We" Betaals...
why do we drink blood?

1181
01:22:36.681 --> 01:22:38.681
Did our ancestors not fancy
any other drink?

1182
01:22:38.973 --> 01:22:41.990
We need to kill humans
to recharge ourselves.

1183
01:22:42.014 --> 01:22:43.014
Ever thought about that?

1184
01:22:43.264 --> 01:22:44.264
No, never.

1185
01:22:45.181 --> 01:22:46.598
We weren't created to kill,

1186
01:22:47.556 --> 01:22:49.223
we were created to protect.

1187
01:22:49.723 --> 01:22:50.723
To protect?

1188
01:22:51.264 --> 01:22:54.348
The great demon Rakhtbeej
had a boon from Lord Shiva.

1189
01:22:55.014 --> 01:23:00.473
Every drop of his blood
would spawn another Rakhtbeej.

1190
01:23:04.306 --> 01:23:07.473
When all the Gods lost to him,

1191
01:23:08.389 --> 01:23:10.223
they turned to the Goddess for help.

1192
01:23:11.556 --> 01:23:14.514
She fought fiercely with Rakhtbeej,

1193
01:23:14.973 --> 01:23:18.973
but every strike that drew his blood

1194
01:23:19.431 --> 01:23:22.764
created more Rakhtbeej.

1195
01:23:24.139 --> 01:23:27.157
So, to kill them and drink their blood,

1196
01:23:27.181 --> 01:23:29.764
the Goddess created Betaal.

1197
01:23:32.431 --> 01:23:35.931
Betaals; born of darkness,

1198
01:23:36.598 --> 01:23:37.824
they drink blood,

1199
01:23:37.848 --> 01:23:39.306
they never die.

1200
01:23:39.681 --> 01:23:42.348
We were created to protect the earth.

1201
01:23:42.681 --> 01:23:46.431
All our rules exist for that.

1202
01:23:46.931 --> 01:23:49.282
Now you must follow them too,

1203
01:23:49.306 --> 01:23:50.848
to protect the earth.

1204
01:23:52.348 --> 01:23:55.348
How the hell am I supposed
to protect anyone when I'm scared stiff?

1205
01:23:55.723 --> 01:23:57.074
How can I protect the entire damn earth?

1206
01:23:57.098 --> 01:23:58.199
What if something happens to me?

1207
01:23:58.223 --> 01:23:58.949
How can I...

1208
01:24:09.098 --> 01:24:10.931
Hey, drop the act...

1209
01:24:11.348 --> 01:24:12.348
you're absolutely fine.

1210
01:24:15.056 --> 01:24:16.139
You'll be indestructible.

1211
01:24:16.556 --> 01:24:17.723
You won't get hurt.

1212
01:24:17.973 --> 01:24:19.056
You won't feel any pain.

1213
01:24:19.348 --> 01:24:20.348
Got it?

1214
01:24:22.681 --> 01:24:24.056
This is crazy!

1215
01:24:25.848 --> 01:24:27.223
I'm slowly getting it.

1216
01:24:28.181 --> 01:24:29.931
You'll go through a lot of changes.

1217
01:24:30.598 --> 01:24:33.223
Now you've got to learn
to control yourself.

1218
01:24:34.348 --> 01:24:35.348
Control.

1219
01:24:37.306 --> 01:24:38.240
Control.

1220
01:24:41.431 --> 01:24:43.514
At first, the sun will bother you,

1221
01:24:43.889 --> 01:24:46.264
stepping out won't be easy.

1222
01:24:46.473 --> 01:24:48.681
But slowly, you'll get used to it.

1223
01:24:48.806 --> 01:24:49.806
Hey!

1224
01:24:50.098 --> 01:24:51.938
Your car's parked all crooked...
straighten it.

1225
01:24:54.139 --> 01:24:56.348
Your strength will grow immensely,

1226
01:24:56.556 --> 01:24:59.014
you won't even realize
how powerful you've become.

1227
01:25:05.973 --> 01:25:08.556
And your speed...
your speed will surpass even a cheetah's.

1228
01:25:18.014 --> 01:25:19.306
See you inside, sir.

1229
01:25:30.389 --> 01:25:33.764
The thirst for blood will grow
every time you see humans.

1230
01:25:34.348 --> 01:25:36.223
But you've got to control it.

1231
01:25:52.764 --> 01:25:53.764
Mummy...

1232
01:26:02.348 --> 01:26:03.348
Alok...

1233
01:26:03.806 --> 01:26:05.056
Alok! Alok!

1234
01:26:05.973 --> 01:26:06.673
Open your mouth!

1235
01:26:06.848 --> 01:26:07.848
Show me your teeth!

1236
01:26:08.889 --> 01:26:11.532
Goyal, flash those punching-machine-like
teeth right now!

1237
01:26:11.556 --> 01:26:12.556
Are you a dentist?

1238
01:26:12.806 --> 01:26:14.490
The other day you wanted to see the mole
on my hip, today you want to see my teeth.

1239
01:26:14.514 --> 01:26:15.449
I'm not showing them. What will you do?

1240
01:26:15.473 --> 01:26:16.806
- I'm out of here.
- Show them!

1241
01:26:20.514 --> 01:26:22.639
Where did they vanish to?

1242
01:26:27.181 --> 01:26:28.848
This is what he does, Inspector!

1243
01:26:29.639 --> 01:26:31.306
My son is a demon.

1244
01:26:32.348 --> 01:26:36.014
That girl turned him into a demon.

1245
01:26:36.598 --> 01:26:39.723
She has got him under her spell.

1246
01:26:40.056 --> 01:26:42.681
She is a witch.

1247
01:26:43.389 --> 01:26:44.389
Come on, Mr. Goyal,

1248
01:26:44.639 --> 01:26:47.199
every in-law claims
their daughter-in-law is a witch.

1249
01:26:47.223 --> 01:26:48.824
She's not even my daughter-in-law.

1250
01:26:48.848 --> 01:26:49.782
Fine, your future daughter-in-law then.

1251
01:26:49.806 --> 01:26:52.223
How's she going to be
that if I don't let her?

1252
01:26:52.514 --> 01:26:55.514
Mr. Goyal, you call your son a demon,

1253
01:26:56.098 --> 01:26:57.556
and your daughter-in-law a witch.

1254
01:26:58.098 --> 01:26:59.098
What about your wife?

1255
01:26:59.181 --> 01:27:00.306
What do you think she is?

1256
01:27:00.973 --> 01:27:02.157
A vengeful spirit?

1257
01:27:05.723 --> 01:27:08.306
Now's not the time to laugh.

1258
01:27:08.681 --> 01:27:10.014
Save my son, please.

1259
01:27:10.473 --> 01:27:11.806
That girl's dangerous.

1260
01:27:12.306 --> 01:27:13.556
She can do anything.

1261
01:27:13.723 --> 01:27:16.532
Obviously, she is a woman.

1262
01:27:16.556 --> 01:27:17.865
Women can do anything.

1263
01:27:17.889 --> 01:27:18.907
But you're the police.

1264
01:27:18.931 --> 01:27:20.251
Aren't you going to do something?

1265
01:27:20.348 --> 01:27:21.348
Of course I am.

1266
01:27:21.848 --> 01:27:22.848
Tell me,

1267
01:27:23.431 --> 01:27:25.240
did you tell anyone else about this?

1268
01:27:25.264 --> 01:27:26.032
No. Not a word.

1269
01:27:26.056 --> 01:27:27.223
Good.

1270
01:27:27.473 --> 01:27:29.973
I'll make sure she's sent away.

1271
01:27:30.223 --> 01:27:32.407
- Go home. P.K.
- P.K.?

1272
01:27:32.431 --> 01:27:34.032
P.K. Yadav, Inspector.

1273
01:27:34.056 --> 01:27:34.848
Yes.

1274
01:27:35.056 --> 01:27:37.264
It's my job to send her away now.

1275
01:27:38.098 --> 01:27:39.498
Fine. It's your responsibility now.

1276
01:27:40.389 --> 01:27:41.389
Okay.

1277
01:27:49.848 --> 01:27:52.740
We have to end the new Betaal
to get Tadaka back.

1278
01:27:52.764 --> 01:27:53.764
No way.

1279
01:27:54.139 --> 01:27:55.139
We can't do that.

1280
01:27:56.139 --> 01:27:58.556
That's against the rules.

1281
01:27:59.223 --> 01:28:03.139
Then maybe it's time to change the rules.

1282
01:28:04.639 --> 01:28:06.639
Only a Thamma can change rules.

1283
01:28:07.264 --> 01:28:08.806
And we've got a Thamma.

1284
01:28:09.139 --> 01:28:10.223
Not our Thamma.

1285
01:28:11.681 --> 01:28:16.723
A Thamma with a heartbeat...

1286
01:28:18.056 --> 01:28:19.848
Only he can lead us forward.

1287
01:28:20.931 --> 01:28:21.931
That's nonsense.

1288
01:28:22.639 --> 01:28:26.931
Humans turn into Betaals
when their heart stops.

1289
01:28:28.181 --> 01:28:29.514
So how can Betaals' hero,

1290
01:28:30.139 --> 01:28:31.139
messiah,

1291
01:28:31.348 --> 01:28:32.348
the new Thamma,

1292
01:28:32.931 --> 01:28:34.306
have a heartbeat?

1293
01:28:35.306 --> 01:28:36.764
That's just folklore.

1294
01:28:37.306 --> 01:28:38.806
No one like that's ever coming.

1295
01:28:39.556 --> 01:28:41.473
Our Thamma's been the same
for centuries...

1296
01:28:42.473 --> 01:28:43.764
The Great Yakshasan.

1297
01:28:50.056 --> 01:28:52.848
Go find Tadaka and that Betaal
and bring them here.

1298
01:29:03.931 --> 01:29:04.931
It's tough, huh?

1299
01:29:05.264 --> 01:29:06.264
I know.

1300
01:29:06.723 --> 01:29:07.723
Really tough.

1301
01:29:07.848 --> 01:29:09.324
- Now jump.
- Okay.

1302
01:29:09.348 --> 01:29:10.348
What?!

1303
01:29:10.639 --> 01:29:11.407
Jump.

1304
01:29:11.431 --> 01:29:12.598
- From here?
- Yes.

1305
01:29:14.931 --> 01:29:15.931
Are you serious?

1306
01:29:43.223 --> 01:29:44.306
What was that?!

1307
01:29:44.598 --> 01:29:46.431
See? You were scared for nothing.

1308
01:29:46.681 --> 01:29:48.074
Me? Scared?
Nah, I don't scare that easily.

1309
01:29:48.098 --> 01:29:49.949
You offered your hand so sweetly that...

1310
01:29:51.264 --> 01:29:52.264
Huh?

1311
01:29:53.264 --> 01:29:53.990
What's this?

1312
01:29:54.014 --> 01:29:55.389
You can't lie anymore.

1313
01:29:57.181 --> 01:29:59.639
Fangs pop out whenever we lie.

1314
01:29:59.889 --> 01:30:00.615
By themselves?

1315
01:30:00.639 --> 01:30:01.639
Uh-huh.

1316
01:30:02.098 --> 01:30:03.378
I can't even bloody lie anymore!

1317
01:30:04.223 --> 01:30:05.681
Control. Control.

1318
01:30:06.181 --> 01:30:07.240
Come on, let's go home.

1319
01:30:07.264 --> 01:30:08.365
Yes, let's go home.

1320
01:30:08.389 --> 01:30:09.431
Not like that.

1321
01:30:09.848 --> 01:30:11.324
How about we hop, skip,
and jump home?

1322
01:30:11.348 --> 01:30:12.348
Hop, skip, and jump?

1323
01:30:28.806 --> 01:30:29.806
I'm good now.

1324
01:30:30.473 --> 01:30:32.098
Could do better.

1325
01:30:32.306 --> 01:30:34.324
There's a lot that's going
to get better now.

1326
01:30:37.931 --> 01:30:39.324
Dad! What are you doing in my room?

1327
01:30:39.348 --> 01:30:40.473
That's so creepy.

1328
01:30:41.098 --> 01:30:42.889
Who's being creepy here, me or you?

1329
01:30:43.348 --> 01:30:44.508
Where did you even come from?

1330
01:30:44.598 --> 01:30:45.598
Outside.

1331
01:30:45.681 --> 01:30:48.032
Everyone comes in from outside, son...

1332
01:30:48.056 --> 01:30:49.490
but through the door.

1333
01:30:49.514 --> 01:30:51.348
Not by jumping in through the balcony.

1334
01:30:51.473 --> 01:30:52.723
Are you stalking me?

1335
01:30:54.181 --> 01:30:55.449
Do you see anything written here?

1336
01:30:55.473 --> 01:30:56.657
Yes. No.

1337
01:30:56.681 --> 01:30:58.473
Then why are you assuming it?

1338
01:30:59.139 --> 01:31:00.619
Tell me, what are you hiding from me?

1339
01:31:01.014 --> 01:31:01.714
Nothing.

1340
01:31:03.431 --> 01:31:04.199
What was that?

1341
01:31:04.223 --> 01:31:05.598
Nothing.
No, no, no...

1342
01:31:06.139 --> 01:31:06.839
Let me see.

1343
01:31:06.848 --> 01:31:08.365
- No. Just drop it.
- Let me see them.

1344
01:31:08.389 --> 01:31:10.139
- Just let it go.
- What's wrong with your nails?

1345
01:31:10.264 --> 01:31:10.964
- Just let it go.
- Let me see them!

1346
01:31:13.681 --> 01:31:16.365
The... the punching-machine-like teeth!

1347
01:31:16.389 --> 01:31:17.990
I was suspicious back at the hospital.

1348
01:31:18.014 --> 01:31:19.223
So I was right.

1349
01:31:20.098 --> 01:31:21.098
What's going on here?

1350
01:31:21.598 --> 01:31:22.931
Your son is dead.

1351
01:31:23.264 --> 01:31:24.115
But he's right here.

1352
01:31:24.139 --> 01:31:27.556
That day, he actually died
in a highway accident.

1353
01:31:29.806 --> 01:31:30.806
He died?

1354
01:31:31.514 --> 01:31:33.139
Then what is this?

1355
01:31:33.348 --> 01:31:34.574
His wandering soul?

1356
01:31:34.598 --> 01:31:35.782
The one that likes to wear a coat?

1357
01:31:35.806 --> 01:31:36.848
He's not a spirit.

1358
01:31:37.056 --> 01:31:38.056
Then?

1359
01:31:38.264 --> 01:31:40.264
I bit him and turned him like me.

1360
01:31:40.556 --> 01:31:41.556
Huh?

1361
01:31:41.764 --> 01:31:42.884
What do you mean "like you"?

1362
01:31:43.723 --> 01:31:44.889
So you're dead too?

1363
01:31:49.723 --> 01:31:53.639
What game are you playing with me?

1364
01:32:10.514 --> 01:32:12.306
My heart doesn't beat, Dad.

1365
01:32:15.848 --> 01:32:16.889
No heartbeat.

1366
01:32:18.556 --> 01:32:22.223
I know you won't believe it,
but it is what it is.

1367
01:32:27.764 --> 01:32:28.806
Aa... Alok...

1368
01:32:31.389 --> 01:32:32.389
Alok...

1369
01:32:35.181 --> 01:32:36.181
Alok...

1370
01:32:38.598 --> 01:32:39.848
My son...

1371
01:32:46.098 --> 01:32:47.098
You...

1372
01:32:47.431 --> 01:32:49.306
You... you're dead?

1373
01:32:53.431 --> 01:32:55.181
If I tell Sudha, she'd...

1374
01:32:59.848 --> 01:33:03.348
We thought you'd support us in old age.

1375
01:33:03.931 --> 01:33:05.056
I will, Dad.

1376
01:33:06.223 --> 01:33:07.663
Now, I'll be your evergreen support.

1377
01:33:08.723 --> 01:33:10.056
You'll grow old,

1378
01:33:10.514 --> 01:33:12.264
but your support will always stay young.

1379
01:33:13.056 --> 01:33:15.598
No, you're not Alok.

1380
01:33:16.598 --> 01:33:18.824
You're my son's spirit. You're not Alok.

1381
01:33:18.848 --> 01:33:20.431
I'm not a spirit, Dad...

1382
01:33:20.973 --> 01:33:22.514
but close.

1383
01:33:24.723 --> 01:33:25.806
I'm a Betaal.

1384
01:33:26.556 --> 01:33:27.556
Betaal?

1385
01:33:28.681 --> 01:33:30.514
That's what our species are called.

1386
01:33:33.264 --> 01:33:34.764
He has turned into a Betaal.

1387
01:33:37.056 --> 01:33:38.181
I knew it!

1388
01:33:38.348 --> 01:33:41.973
I knew you "witch"
would spell doom for my son!

1389
01:33:42.514 --> 01:33:45.264
If I hadn't done this,
he'd have died in the hospital.

1390
01:33:46.389 --> 01:33:48.306
I couldn't let him die.

1391
01:33:50.520 --> 01:33:52.098
I love Alok.

1392
01:33:53.306 --> 01:33:55.348
Couldn't you love someone else?

1393
01:33:56.264 --> 01:33:58.431
You should've chosen someone
from your own community.

1394
01:33:59.014 --> 01:34:01.306
Some tall, dark, red-eyed guy with fangs.

1395
01:34:03.848 --> 01:34:05.306
Don't worry, son.

1396
01:34:05.889 --> 01:34:07.764
I'll get the best doctor.

1397
01:34:08.306 --> 01:34:09.865
I'll get the best heart doctor,

1398
01:34:09.889 --> 01:34:13.639
transplant your heart,
bring your heartbeat back.

1399
01:34:13.973 --> 01:34:15.306
Doctors can't help, Dad.

1400
01:34:15.431 --> 01:34:20.032
If not a doctor, then a tantric
or miracle performing sage could help.

1401
01:34:20.056 --> 01:34:21.431
No one can do anything, Dad.

1402
01:34:22.598 --> 01:34:23.723
Not even God.

1403
01:34:26.931 --> 01:34:30.098
How about the hand of God?

1404
01:34:30.764 --> 01:34:31.764
Hmm?

1405
01:34:32.306 --> 01:34:33.306
Don't worry, son.

1406
01:34:33.889 --> 01:34:36.556
The hand of God is with youuuu.

1407
01:34:36.889 --> 01:34:38.931
Why don't you get it?

1408
01:34:40.139 --> 01:34:41.598
How do I explain?

1409
01:34:42.473 --> 01:34:44.848
I'll tell you a story. Listen carefully.

1410
01:34:45.223 --> 01:34:49.365
It's a full moon night,
moonlight falls on the earth...

1411
01:34:49.389 --> 01:34:51.181
And the moment it hits, my brother goes...

1412
01:34:55.306 --> 01:34:56.306
Grrrr!

1413
01:34:56.598 --> 01:34:57.598
Grrrr?!

1414
01:34:57.681 --> 01:34:58.931
Grrrr!

1415
01:34:59.806 --> 01:35:01.865
Oh my God,
your brother's a Bhediya!

1416
01:35:01.889 --> 01:35:03.532
Exactly!

1417
01:35:03.556 --> 01:35:05.032
Yes! Yes! Yes!

1418
01:35:05.056 --> 01:35:05.865
Yes.

1419
01:35:05.889 --> 01:35:08.723
He's a perverted human,
with a wolf inside.

1420
01:35:09.056 --> 01:35:11.740
Amazing! We desperately need a Bhediya.

1421
01:35:11.764 --> 01:35:12.764
Okay.

1422
01:35:13.848 --> 01:35:14.973
Tell me,

1423
01:35:16.473 --> 01:35:18.433
how exactly did your brother
turn into a Bhediya?

1424
01:35:18.639 --> 01:35:20.032
Long story.

1425
01:35:20.056 --> 01:35:22.324
You could easily make a movie
with a post-credit scene out of it.

1426
01:35:22.348 --> 01:35:23.490
I'll tell you some other time.

1427
01:35:23.514 --> 01:35:25.074
Right now, I am here because
he's dealing with a big problem.

1428
01:35:25.098 --> 01:35:25.990
So just hear me out.

1429
01:35:26.014 --> 01:35:28.348
Why are you here instead of him?

1430
01:35:29.223 --> 01:35:34.306
He's been thrashed so badly,
he can't face anyone anymore.

1431
01:35:34.723 --> 01:35:37.056
Impossible! Bhediya is so powerful!

1432
01:35:37.306 --> 01:35:38.598
Who thrashed him?

1433
01:35:39.389 --> 01:35:43.389
A monster... with a chopped off thingy.

1434
01:35:43.514 --> 01:35:44.681
With a chopped off what?

1435
01:35:44.973 --> 01:35:46.389
A chopped-off body part.

1436
01:35:47.098 --> 01:35:48.098
During the fight,

1437
01:35:48.598 --> 01:35:51.806
that monster did things I can't even say.

1438
01:35:53.431 --> 01:35:54.532
He did that?

1439
01:35:54.556 --> 01:35:56.139
No, he didn't do THAT!

1440
01:35:56.598 --> 01:35:59.181
Come on, man!
My brother fought the monster.

1441
01:35:59.389 --> 01:36:01.098
So the monster thrashed him so badly...

1442
01:36:01.473 --> 01:36:02.514
How did he thrash him?

1443
01:36:02.681 --> 01:36:03.681
Like this.

1444
01:36:07.806 --> 01:36:09.990
Now that poor guy
can't fully turn into a Bhediya.

1445
01:36:10.014 --> 01:36:11.931
All he can do is... Dame Un Grrr!

1446
01:36:12.889 --> 01:36:14.306
You're quite skilled.

1447
01:36:14.723 --> 01:36:16.973
You helped capture that wretched Munjya.

1448
01:36:17.764 --> 01:36:19.949
You've got a solution for this too, right?

1449
01:36:19.973 --> 01:36:22.139
Any powder, pill, elixir of life?
Anything?

1450
01:36:22.431 --> 01:36:24.306
Think with your mind, not your hand.

1451
01:36:26.431 --> 01:36:27.431
Stop it.

1452
01:36:31.431 --> 01:36:32.324
Hey, Padre!

1453
01:36:33.431 --> 01:36:34.473
Padre, my brother?

1454
01:36:41.306 --> 01:36:42.473
Hey!

1455
01:36:45.806 --> 01:36:47.115
That's my brother! That's my brother!

1456
01:36:47.139 --> 01:36:49.264
Yes, Bhediya:

1457
01:36:49.848 --> 01:36:51.699
- The protector of the jungle!
- Right.

1458
01:36:51.723 --> 01:36:55.931
To boost his power, he needs
to drink the blood

1459
01:36:56.931 --> 01:36:58.306
of a bloodsucker.

1460
01:36:58.556 --> 01:36:59.764
A bloodsucker?

1461
01:37:00.348 --> 01:37:01.907
A leech! You mean a leech!

1462
01:37:07.139 --> 01:37:08.389
No,

1463
01:37:09.139 --> 01:37:10.889
I mean a special species.

1464
01:37:11.473 --> 01:37:15.139
They look like humans
and drink human blood.

1465
01:37:17.348 --> 01:37:18.598
Betaal!

1466
01:37:20.681 --> 01:37:25.740
He sinks his fangs right into the vein
and drinks the blood.

1467
01:37:25.764 --> 01:37:26.490
Yes.

1468
01:37:26.514 --> 01:37:27.764
Like Dracula?

1469
01:37:28.139 --> 01:37:29.139
Something like that.

1470
01:37:29.973 --> 01:37:32.139
But that species is extinct.

1471
01:37:32.264 --> 01:37:34.348
Extinct? No, don't say that.

1472
01:37:38.098 --> 01:37:39.973
Sorry, It looks difficult.

1473
01:37:40.306 --> 01:37:41.990
You keep shouting,
"Hand of God! Hand of God!"

1474
01:37:42.014 --> 01:37:43.306
You've got to do something.

1475
01:37:43.764 --> 01:37:44.657
Don't you know that

1476
01:37:44.681 --> 01:37:47.240
the glaciers are melting
and extinct species are coming back?

1477
01:37:47.264 --> 01:37:50.264
Huge tusked elephants, flying crocodiles,
good actors.

1478
01:37:51.056 --> 01:37:52.973
Padre, please, just two minutes.

1479
01:37:53.139 --> 01:37:54.139
Just two minutes.

1480
01:37:54.639 --> 01:37:55.907
- What happened?
- There's an emergency.

1481
01:37:55.931 --> 01:37:56.824
What's the emergency?

1482
01:37:56.848 --> 01:37:58.598
Am I invisible or what?

1483
01:37:58.764 --> 01:38:00.032
I'm still sitting here talking to him,
and you just barged in!

1484
01:38:00.056 --> 01:38:01.490
A desperate father is begging you.

1485
01:38:01.514 --> 01:38:03.365
Only two minutes.
Please.

1486
01:38:03.389 --> 01:38:06.389
No, Uncle, don't. You can take three.

1487
01:38:07.431 --> 01:38:08.764
Thank you, son, thank you.

1488
01:38:10.264 --> 01:38:12.098
Bittu! What are you doing in Delhi, bro?

1489
01:38:13.223 --> 01:38:14.223
Who's Bittu?

1490
01:38:21.098 --> 01:38:23.657
Now, what's the emergency?

1491
01:38:23.681 --> 01:38:24.889
The emergency...

1492
01:38:25.181 --> 01:38:29.699
Sir, there's a boy who a witchy girl...

1493
01:38:29.723 --> 01:38:31.973
- Dad...
- Give me a minute, let me explain.

1494
01:38:33.348 --> 01:38:40.306
A boy was bitten here by a witchy girl.

1495
01:38:41.556 --> 01:38:44.723
Now he's become like her.

1496
01:38:45.264 --> 01:38:46.264
Sex change?

1497
01:38:46.389 --> 01:38:48.240
No, no, no sex change.

1498
01:38:48.264 --> 01:38:51.973
He's turned into a demon, just like her.

1499
01:38:52.598 --> 01:38:54.056
His heart doesn't beat.

1500
01:38:54.431 --> 01:38:55.973
He gets wild at the sight of blood.

1501
01:38:56.514 --> 01:38:58.973
He's dead, yet alive.

1502
01:39:00.389 --> 01:39:02.139
You are talking about him, right?

1503
01:39:02.389 --> 01:39:04.324
No sir, he's talking about someone else.

1504
01:39:05.931 --> 01:39:07.889
Hey! Hey Betaal!

1505
01:39:10.264 --> 01:39:11.264
Miracle!

1506
01:39:11.473 --> 01:39:12.306
Miracle!

1507
01:39:12.431 --> 01:39:13.282
Miracle!

1508
01:39:13.306 --> 01:39:16.598
What a coincidence!

1509
01:39:16.723 --> 01:39:18.199
- You know about them?
- Yes.

1510
01:39:18.223 --> 01:39:21.282
I knew it! I knew you'd know!

1511
01:39:21.306 --> 01:39:23.282
So tell me Padre,

1512
01:39:23.306 --> 01:39:26.473
is there any way to cure a Betaal
and make him human again?

1513
01:39:27.264 --> 01:39:29.556
You can make an omelette
from an egg, right?

1514
01:39:29.764 --> 01:39:30.806
Right.

1515
01:39:31.139 --> 01:39:33.431
But can an omelette ever turn back
into an egg?

1516
01:39:34.098 --> 01:39:35.889
I wouldn't know... I'm vegetarian.

1517
01:39:36.389 --> 01:39:37.473
Oh.

1518
01:39:38.139 --> 01:39:41.139
Then... You can make
ketchup from tomatoes, right?

1519
01:39:41.389 --> 01:39:42.240
Right.

1520
01:39:42.264 --> 01:39:44.431
But can ketchup ever turn back
into tomatoes?

1521
01:39:44.639 --> 01:39:46.324
- No. No way.
- No.

1522
01:39:46.348 --> 01:39:49.431
Similarly, human to Betaal, possible.

1523
01:39:50.098 --> 01:39:51.639
But Betaal to human...

1524
01:39:52.764 --> 01:39:53.764
impossible.

1525
01:39:55.681 --> 01:39:56.889
Don't say that.

1526
01:39:57.639 --> 01:39:59.181
Don't say it, please.

1527
01:39:59.639 --> 01:40:01.348
You don't say that.

1528
01:40:01.848 --> 01:40:02.973
Be happy.

1529
01:40:04.098 --> 01:40:05.407
Congratulations.

1530
01:40:05.431 --> 01:40:06.431
For what?

1531
01:40:07.056 --> 01:40:10.806
Your family's light can't be extinguished
even with a fire extinguisher.

1532
01:40:11.264 --> 01:40:12.556
He's immortal.

1533
01:40:12.723 --> 01:40:15.848
You're our last hope.

1534
01:40:16.181 --> 01:40:17.365
Please save him.

1535
01:40:17.389 --> 01:40:18.431
Please.

1536
01:40:18.764 --> 01:40:19.931
Please save him.

1537
01:40:20.348 --> 01:40:22.056
I can understand your feelings.

1538
01:40:23.348 --> 01:40:25.431
But I am telling you
with all my experience...

1539
01:40:26.223 --> 01:40:27.556
Nothing can be done.

1540
01:40:29.181 --> 01:40:30.223
Accept it.

1541
01:40:31.431 --> 01:40:32.681
There is no cure?

1542
01:40:35.389 --> 01:40:36.389
No chance.

1543
01:40:40.639 --> 01:40:41.639
Alok?

1544
01:40:41.931 --> 01:40:42.931
Goyal?

1545
01:40:43.764 --> 01:40:45.115
- Goyal?!
- Greetings, Uncle.

1546
01:40:45.139 --> 01:40:47.179
Sir, don't forget
to transfer my fees of Rs. 10,000!

1547
01:40:47.431 --> 01:40:48.473
Alok, listen...

1548
01:40:48.723 --> 01:40:50.764
Why should I listen to you?
Why should I, huh?

1549
01:40:51.598 --> 01:40:56.098
The girl you call a witch
and demon gave me a new life.

1550
01:40:56.973 --> 01:40:59.139
And your son loves her.

1551
01:41:00.181 --> 01:41:01.389
And he always will.

1552
01:41:06.848 --> 01:41:08.008
That's no way to call anyone.

1553
01:41:08.098 --> 01:41:09.806
I have a name - Jana, JD, Janardhan.

1554
01:41:11.264 --> 01:41:12.264
What is it?

1555
01:41:15.014 --> 01:41:15.714
What?

1556
01:41:18.639 --> 01:41:19.639
What are you saying?

1557
01:41:26.806 --> 01:41:28.306
Thank you, Padre. Thank you.

1558
01:41:31.723 --> 01:41:32.723
Gift!

1559
01:41:33.639 --> 01:41:35.348
Make your brother sniff it.

1560
01:41:36.556 --> 01:41:37.556
Elixir of life.

1561
01:41:37.973 --> 01:41:39.032
- Yes.
- Yes.

1562
01:41:39.056 --> 01:41:40.181
Okay.

1563
01:41:40.306 --> 01:41:43.014
Miracle! Miracle! Miracle! Miracle!

1564
01:42:13.931 --> 01:42:15.699
Mom, give the phone to Tarika.

1565
01:42:15.723 --> 01:42:16.740
Okay, hang on.

1566
01:42:16.764 --> 01:42:17.764
Alok.

1567
01:42:19.473 --> 01:42:21.098
Tarika, listen up.

1568
01:42:21.556 --> 01:42:24.365
Those guys from your tribe who were
chasing us in the jungle the other day...

1569
01:42:24.389 --> 01:42:25.389
they're here.

1570
01:42:25.931 --> 01:42:26.824
They're following me.

1571
01:42:26.848 --> 01:42:29.282
Alok, get out of there now.

1572
01:42:29.306 --> 01:42:31.115
Get to high ground, I'm on my way.

1573
01:42:31.139 --> 01:42:32.556
Okay.

1574
01:42:50.556 --> 01:42:51.657
Hey, are you blind of what?

1575
01:42:52.098 --> 01:42:53.098
Hey!

1576
01:42:53.348 --> 01:42:54.348
Hey!

1577
01:44:11.598 --> 01:44:13.139
Who the hell are you?

1578
01:44:13.598 --> 01:44:14.949
And why'd you fling that rag in my face?

1579
01:44:14.973 --> 01:44:15.973
Forget the rag...

1580
01:44:16.306 --> 01:44:18.181
I know all about you.

1581
01:44:18.514 --> 01:44:19.514
What...

1582
01:44:19.931 --> 01:44:20.865
what do you know?

1583
01:44:20.889 --> 01:44:22.973
I know you're a Betaal.

1584
01:44:24.014 --> 01:44:25.056
Doesn't matter who I am.

1585
01:44:25.723 --> 01:44:27.098
What do you want, bro?

1586
01:44:27.764 --> 01:44:29.139
Your blood.

1587
01:44:29.473 --> 01:44:31.556
Oh, you Wannabe Wolverine,

1588
01:44:31.806 --> 01:44:33.282
you're going to resort
to bloodshed now, huh?

1589
01:44:33.306 --> 01:44:36.348
Hey Dracula on a budget!

1590
01:44:37.014 --> 01:44:39.389
I will drink your blood today.

1591
01:44:41.556 --> 01:44:42.532
What's with the overacting?

1592
01:44:42.556 --> 01:44:44.139
Who's overacting, huh?

1593
01:45:41.806 --> 01:45:42.889
Cut the crap.

1594
01:45:43.431 --> 01:45:44.806
Let me have your blood, or else...

1595
01:45:45.014 --> 01:45:46.454
Why the hell do you even want blood?

1596
01:45:46.889 --> 01:45:48.431
I'm the one who drinks blood here.

1597
01:46:10.348 --> 01:46:12.389
Look, I'm asking nicely.

1598
01:46:13.514 --> 01:46:14.639
Let me have your blood.

1599
01:46:15.848 --> 01:46:16.848
Oh, you want my blood?

1600
01:46:26.556 --> 01:46:27.556
Then come here...

1601
01:46:28.223 --> 01:46:29.223
and take it yourself.

1602
01:46:34.556 --> 01:46:35.556
Tommy...

1603
01:46:37.139 --> 01:46:38.181
Come on.

1604
01:47:53.556 --> 01:48:01.556
I am... I am Bhediya!

1605
01:48:13.889 --> 01:48:17.074
I came from the jungle
to shake up the town,

1606
01:48:17.098 --> 01:48:20.764
With blood-soaked fangs,
I'll strike them down.

1607
01:48:21.598 --> 01:48:24.324
I'll hunt you down,
no one can save you from me,

1608
01:48:24.348 --> 01:48:27.681
Now I tear through bone,
along with flesh with glee.

1609
01:48:30.264 --> 01:48:31.514
Cut it out, bro.

1610
01:48:31.889 --> 01:48:33.056
That's enough.

1611
01:48:35.889 --> 01:48:38.889
Under moonlit skies, I vanish to shadow,

1612
01:48:45.264 --> 01:48:48.490
From jungle to towers, I prowl unseen,

1613
01:48:48.514 --> 01:48:52.032
Who dares face this beast so mean?

1614
01:48:52.056 --> 01:48:55.723
No one survives me,
I am such a catastrophe,

1615
01:49:41.806 --> 01:49:42.848
Who's this guy?

1616
01:49:43.223 --> 01:49:44.282
- I don't know.
- You don't know?

1617
01:49:44.306 --> 01:49:45.240
I don't.

1618
01:49:45.264 --> 01:49:46.431
You can kill him, right?

1619
01:49:46.764 --> 01:49:48.348
Ye... No! No!

1620
01:49:48.514 --> 01:49:49.806
What kind of a Betaal are you?

1621
01:49:50.098 --> 01:49:51.098
Yes.

1622
01:49:53.223 --> 01:49:54.074
What do we do now?

1623
01:49:54.098 --> 01:49:55.181
What do we do?

1624
01:49:58.223 --> 01:49:59.223
Let's go.

1625
01:50:06.598 --> 01:50:08.514
What the hell?

1626
01:50:08.973 --> 01:50:12.615
This... is... crazy!

1627
01:50:12.639 --> 01:50:17.348
Who am I?! I must be dreaming!

1628
01:50:59.056 --> 01:51:03.931
All through the jungle,
word is spreading, news is heading!

1629
01:51:04.181 --> 01:51:09.324
Hey! A flower has bloomed
without his underwear!

1630
01:51:09.348 --> 01:51:11.574
- Hey! A flower has bloomed
- Jana!

1631
01:51:11.598 --> 01:51:14.431
Without his underwear!

1632
01:51:14.806 --> 01:51:15.973
Why did you drag me here?

1633
01:51:19.723 --> 01:51:21.074
He's the one who'll spill everything.

1634
01:51:27.681 --> 01:51:28.574
Tadaka?

1635
01:51:28.598 --> 01:51:30.056
What's he doing here?

1636
01:51:30.389 --> 01:51:31.473
He...

1637
01:51:31.723 --> 01:51:32.824
Rakhtrambha!

1638
01:51:32.848 --> 01:51:34.931
Sasakhtrambha!

1639
01:51:40.014 --> 01:51:41.139
Oh.

1640
01:51:42.848 --> 01:51:44.723
You too?

1641
01:51:47.889 --> 01:51:48.973
He's a cop.

1642
01:51:49.889 --> 01:51:50.889
How can he...?

1643
01:51:51.431 --> 01:51:52.931
What have you done?

1644
01:51:53.306 --> 01:51:54.848
This is a disaster.

1645
01:51:55.056 --> 01:51:56.098
You bit him.

1646
01:51:56.306 --> 01:51:57.907
I told you to leave, didn't I?

1647
01:51:57.931 --> 01:51:59.764
Do you even know what you've done?
You could...

1648
01:52:00.306 --> 01:52:01.764
I know. Everything.

1649
01:52:03.139 --> 01:52:05.681
Mr. Yadav, we came for your help.

1650
01:52:05.973 --> 01:52:06.973
What happened?

1651
01:52:07.056 --> 01:52:09.264
Some weird guy attacked me.

1652
01:52:10.139 --> 01:52:12.931
He's got fangs and long nails like ours.
He's beefed up.

1653
01:52:13.056 --> 01:52:14.848
Moves like an animal-like this.

1654
01:52:15.806 --> 01:52:16.806
Archenemies.

1655
01:52:18.014 --> 01:52:19.014
Virus.

1656
01:52:19.306 --> 01:52:20.306
Yapum.

1657
01:52:20.514 --> 01:52:21.514
Bhediya.

1658
01:52:22.139 --> 01:52:23.157
Where'd you see him?

1659
01:52:23.181 --> 01:52:24.865
Here.
How does it matter anyway?

1660
01:52:24.889 --> 01:52:26.574
And why would I even be his enemy?

1661
01:52:26.598 --> 01:52:28.556
Not just you, all of us are.

1662
01:52:28.848 --> 01:52:30.014
It's ancestral thing.

1663
01:52:30.723 --> 01:52:32.643
They've been thirsty
for our blood for centuries.

1664
01:52:33.931 --> 01:52:35.514
He didn't drink your blood, did he?

1665
01:52:36.764 --> 01:52:38.306
He wouldn't dare.

1666
01:52:38.889 --> 01:52:41.240
I offered a drop upfront.

1667
01:52:41.264 --> 01:52:43.014
I said, "Here, son, enjoy."

1668
01:52:44.014 --> 01:52:47.056
You idiot! You fool! You dumbo!

1669
01:52:48.348 --> 01:52:50.389
Couldn't you pick anyone else to bite?

1670
01:52:51.348 --> 01:52:52.240
What's wrong?

1671
01:52:52.264 --> 01:52:53.240
This is a catastrophe.

1672
01:52:53.264 --> 01:52:54.264
What's wrong, she asks!

1673
01:52:54.598 --> 01:52:58.615
One drop of Betaal blood makes
Bhediya ten times deadlier.

1674
01:52:58.639 --> 01:52:59.639
Ten times!

1675
01:53:00.348 --> 01:53:02.306
Now he'll hunt him like a maniac.

1676
01:53:02.556 --> 01:53:06.181
He won't rest till he drains him dry.

1677
01:53:08.348 --> 01:53:09.598
I won't let him get hurt.

1678
01:53:09.973 --> 01:53:12.348
He'll crush you like an ant. An ant!

1679
01:53:14.348 --> 01:53:16.348
I told you to leave.

1680
01:53:16.848 --> 01:53:18.615
You've messed up the balance.

1681
01:53:18.639 --> 01:53:20.348
Tarika, you've broken the balance.

1682
01:53:20.473 --> 01:53:21.764
Now what do I tell them?

1683
01:53:22.348 --> 01:53:23.639
What do I tell them, huh?

1684
01:53:25.056 --> 01:53:26.431
We're all in danger now.

1685
01:53:27.056 --> 01:53:28.056
All of us.

1686
01:53:30.556 --> 01:53:31.681
Listen carefully.

1687
01:53:32.306 --> 01:53:34.639
I and my crew will have to protect him.

1688
01:53:35.056 --> 01:53:36.056
Your crew?

1689
01:53:36.431 --> 01:53:37.911
Come with me, I'll show you the crew.

1690
01:53:38.473 --> 01:53:40.098
But... not like that.

1691
01:53:40.764 --> 01:53:41.889
These clothes won't cut it.

1692
01:54:00.639 --> 01:54:01.931
Welcome to our world.

1693
01:54:02.473 --> 01:54:04.514
Don't worry, everyone here's just like us.

1694
01:54:04.931 --> 01:54:05.931
Yes.

1695
01:54:07.806 --> 01:54:08.806
Amazing.

1696
01:54:09.764 --> 01:54:11.074
Wait till I show you something
even crazier inside.

1697
01:54:11.098 --> 01:54:12.139
Come.

1698
01:54:22.306 --> 01:54:24.014
Look at our treasure.

1699
01:54:24.348 --> 01:54:25.240
All those bottles contain blood?

1700
01:54:25.264 --> 01:54:26.848
The rarest of the rare.

1701
01:54:28.556 --> 01:54:29.764
Try this.

1702
01:54:30.889 --> 01:54:31.973
Whose blood is it?

1703
01:54:38.306 --> 01:54:42.407
One who never beheld his beloved's gaze,

1704
